      "detailed_desc": "In this congenic strain, the DBA/2 H2 complex (H2d), including the nonclassical class 1 T18c (thymus leukemia (TL) antigen) loci, on chromosome 17 was introgressed onto the C57BL/10Sn background. H2d occurs naturally in the following inbred strains: DBA/2, DBA/2J BALB/c, BALB/cByJ, BALB/cJ, C57BLKS, NZB. The H2d haplotype is d at the class I loci (K, D) and the class II loci (A, E). This strain carries the hemolytic complement or C5 sufficient (Hc1) allele from C57BL/10Sn in contrast to B10.D2-Hc0 H2d H2-T18c/oSnJ (Stock # 000461), in which, Hc0 has a 2 base pair deletion that generates a stop codon. Mice congenic for H2 haplotypes are widely used in immunologic research and often vary in immune response and pathogen susceptibility from the recipient strain. 分子注记：This allele does not contain the 2 base \"TA\" deletion found in the Hc0 allele and is found in the following mouse strains BALB/cJ, C57BL/6J, DBA/1J, and B10.D2/nSnJ. This is equivalent to the wild-type allele. The allele H2-T18c determines presence of specificities TL.2, 7 and occurs in strains BALB/c, DBA/2, 129/J, and others."
