      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote; HOMOZYGOUS X WILD AND RECIP Coat color: Black Generation: N8+pN1F3",
      "detailed_desc": "The E326K coding variant (current nomenclature E365K) of the human GBA1 (glucosidase, beta, acid 1) gene on chromosome 1q22 is potentially associated with increased susceptibility to familial Parkinson's disease (PMID:28830825). Gba1E326K mice carry a corresponding E344K (GAG to AAG) knock-in and 2 silent mutations in exon 8 of the mouse Gba1 gene. Homozygotes show ~30-40% reduction in GCase activity in whole brain tissue as well as a decrease in the total protein. They are viable and fertile and without overt phenotype. This strain has not as yet been published and studies are ongoing. We will update this description as more information becomes known. (February, 2022) Distribution of this strain was supported by the Michael J. Fox Foundation for Parkinson's Research. 分子注记：CRISPR/Cas9 methodologies is used to incorporate an E344K (also designated E326K) (GAG to AAG) knock-in in exon 8 (NM_001077411.4) and 2 silent mutations: wildtype CCAAAGCTACTTTAGGAGAGACA to mutant CtAAgGCcACTTTAGGAAAGACA. This mutation corresponds to a human coding variant potentially associated with increased susceptibility to familial ParkinsonÃ¢Â€Â™s disease."
