      "breeding_summary": "Mating scheme: Sibling x Sibling Coat color: Black Generation: N9F122pF5",
      "detailed_desc": "In approximately 2003 some phenotypic parameters of the B10.BR-H2k2 H2-T18a/SgSnJ mice were found to have changed relative to the strain's previous performance. In order to confirm that a change had occurred and in order to better characterize any differences that may have arisen, animals were recovered from cryopreserved embryos of the strain (Stock No. 004804) that had been frozen in 1991, and the two lines of B10.BR-H2k2 H2-T18a/SgSnJ were compared. Stock #465, which has been continuously on the shelf shows a shift in the CD4/CD8 T cell ratios to an increased percentage of CD8 postitive T cells. Accompanying this change is an increase in splenic leukocyte cellularity and a conspicuous elevation in cells of the monocyte lineage. Both colonies of B10.BR-H2k2 H2-T18a/SgSnJ (Stock No's. 000465 and 004804) may exhibit white belly spots; these spots are considered a strain characteristic. 分子注记：The H2k2 haplotype differs from the prototype H2k in having the a, rather than the canonical b, alleles of the Class Ib genes T18 (formerly Tla) and Qa-1. The H2k2 haplotype is shared by the inbred strains C57BR/cdJ and C58/J and the H2 congenic strain B10.BR-H2k2 H2-T18a/SgSnJ (formerly B10.BR-H2k/SgSnJ). The allele H2-T18a determines presence of the antigenic specificities TL.1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 7 and occurs in strains A, C57BR, C58, SJL, and others."
