      "breeding_summary": "Mice are maintained as homozygotes for the H2r and H2-T18b alleles. Intervals near markers D10Mit96, D15Mit111, and D14Mit135 that have been associated with the collagen-induced arthritis phenotype (PMID: 15761851) are segregating for both C57BL/10Sn and RIII sequences in this colony. &nbsp;Wean-aged mice may show signs of barbering that include whisker picking. Affected mice typically regrow whiskers within two weeks after weaning. Mating scheme: Sibling x Sibling Coat color: Black Generation: Contact Technical Support",
      "detailed_desc": "The B10.RIII congenic stain was developed by Dr. George Snell and Dr. Marianna Cherry in the 1960's. The RIII inbred strain was crossed to inbred C57BL/10Sn mice and progeny were backcrossed to C57BL/10Sn mice for a total of 8 backcross generations to create the original line. Animals were selected at each generation by serotyping with anti-H2r antisera. Additional backcrosses to C57BL/10SnJ (Stock No.&nbsp;000666) were subsequently carried out in this colony. Approximate pedigree generation numbers and dates: N8F77 October, 1992; N8F117 November, 2005; N8F128 January, 2010; N8F138 September, 2013; N8F142 August, 2014; N9 April, 2016; N10 August; 2017, N11F3 April, 2018. Intervals near markers D10Mit96, D15Mit111, and D14Mit135 that have been associated with the collagen-induced arthritis phenotype (PMID: 15761851) are segregating for both C57BL/10Sn and RIII sequences in this colony. Please see Stock No. 037494 B10.RIII 2J for mice that are homozygous for the RIII-derived intervals. No phenotypic differences between Stock No. 000457 and Stock No. 037494 have been documented, as yet (April, 2025). 分子注记：The allele H2-T18b determines absence of the antigen (TL-) and occurs in strains C57BL/6, AKR, C3H/An, and many others."
