      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N2+pN2\t",
      "detailed_desc": "The hAbetaSAA (APP-SAA KI) knock-in mouse model of Alzheimer's disease (AD) carries humanizing A&beta; region R684H, F681Y, and G676R mutations, and the KM670/671NL (Swedish) mutation in exon 16 as well as the E693G (Arctic) and T714I (Austrian) mutations in exon 17 of the mouse App (amyloid beta (A4) precursor protein) gene. Mice recapitulate amyloid plaque pathology in vivo without disturbing intrinsic gene expression. As a control, we recommend the hAbeta model (Stock No. 033013), which has the same humanized Abeta region but lacks the three familial AD mutations. Also see: Alzforum (February 6, 2021). 分子注记：The targeting vector was used to introduce the human R684H, F681Y, G676R and KM670/671NL (Swedish) mutations into to exon 16. An FRT-flanked PGK-neomycin cassette (in reverse transcriptional orientation), and an F3-flanked PGK-hygromycin cassette (in reverse transcriptional orientation) is placed in intron 16, and the E693G (Artic) and T714I (Austrian) mutations are introduced to exon 17. Flpe-mediated recombination removed the FRT-flanked neomycin and hygromycin cassettes."
