      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, hemizygous mice may be bred together, to wildtype siblings, or to C57BL/6NJ inbred mice (Stock No. 005304). It should be noted that homozygous females fail to mate successfully. Mating scheme: Noncarrier x Hemizygote; Hemizygote x Noncarrier Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN2F5",
      "detailed_desc": "PS19 transgenic mice (P301S Tg mice) express the P301S mutant form of human microtubule-associated protein tau (MAPT), under the direction of the mouse prion protein promoter (Prnp). The expression of the mutant human MAPT is five-fold higher than the expression of the endogenous mouse MAPT protein. Hyperphosphorylated, insoluble mutant human MAPT protein in the brain accumulates with age causing decreased microtubule binding. The donating laboratory confirmed the following phenotype for these C57BL/6-congenic PS19 transgenic mice [March 2014]: Transgenic mice have a median lifespan between 11 and 15 months. 13 week old mice are hyperactive and exhibit decreased anxiety-like behavior. By 6 months of age, motor weakness is observed. Transgenic mice have lowered thresholds in nociceptive response (hot plate test) and startle response (prepulse inhibition), as well as memory deficits. Histological analysis reveals phosphorylated tau accumulation in the lateral globus pallidus, amygdala, auditory cortex, and ventral hippocampus. Onset of neuronal loss occurs at approximately nine months of age. Transgenic mice on the congenic C57BL/6 are less variable than transgenic mice on the mixed B6;C3 background in the onset of hyperphosphorylated tau inclusions, neuronal loss, and death. Note that Takeuchi et al. 2011 PLoS One 6:e21050 describes PS19 transgenic mice N10 onto C57BL/6J, whereas Stock No. 024841 is N7+ onto C57BL/6N (see strain Development section). These mice cannot be bred to homozygosity as homozygous females do not mate. 分子注记：The transgene construct contains the P301S mutant human microtubule-associated protein tau, MAPT, under the direction of the mouse prion protein, Prnp, promoter. The expression of the mutant human MAPT is 5-fold higher than the expression of the endogenous mouse Mapt protein. Transgene insertion occurred on Chr 3, causing a 249 Kb deletion."
