      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, these mice can be bred as homozygotes. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN2F4",
      "detailed_desc": "hAbeta-loxP-KI knock-in is a mutant \"humanized\" App allele in which three mutations were introduced into the mouse App exon that encodes the A&beta; fragment (see below), such that the sequence now encodes the same amino acids as human. This exon is also flanked by loxP sites. These hAbeta-loxP-KI mice express mouse APP protein with a \"humanized\" amyloid beta peptide sequence. Homozygotes are viable and fertile. As the mice are characterized, we will modify the strain description and add phenotype data. Important note about App isoforms and exon numbering: The App-201 isoform (695 aa protein) is encoded by 16 exons, of which the Abeta sequence is encoded by exon 14. The App-206 isoform (770 aa protein) is encoded by 18 exons, of which the Abeta sequence is encoded by exon 16. The hAbeta-loxP-KI allele is available on a C57BL/6J congenic background (Stock No. 031050), on a C57BL/6NJ congenic background (Stock No. 032013) and on a mixed C57BL/6J and C57BL/6NJ background (Stock No. 030898). 分子注记：The targeting construct includes a loxP site upstream of exon 16 of App-206 isoform, 3 point mutations inserted into exon 14 to create amino acid substitutions (amino acids 5 (G->R), 10 (F->Y) and 13 (R->H)) (ENSMUSE00000131684), a loxP site downstream of exon 16 and a FRT-flanked neo selection cassette, which is removed by FLP-mediated recombination."
