      "breeding_summary": "Mice homozygous for the mutation are viable and fertile and can be used for breeding. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Amyloid beta (A4) precursor protein (APP) is a type I integral membrane protein that is cleaved to form a number of peptides, in particular, the amyloid-&beta;-peptide, a component of the amyloid plaques associated with Alzheimer's disease. These humanized App knock-in/knock-out mice carry a 350 kb fragment of human APP replacing the mouse App locus. Mice homozygous for the mutation are viable and fertile. These mice may be useful for studying APP function and late onset Alzheimer's disease. 分子注记：The targeting vector is designed to insert a 343 kb (Chr21:25880264 - 26224036) fragment of the human APP (apolipoprotein) in place of 268 kb (Chr16:84750107 - 85019011) of the mouse App gene. The construct includes an FRT-flanked neomycin selection cassette. In addition, there is also a APP-DT (non-coding antisense RNA) in the human genome segment. The insertion disrupts App transcription.The neomycin cassette was removed by transient expression of cre."
