      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes are viable and fertile. Homozygous matings have been unproductive in The Jackson Laboratory colony. Mating scheme: Wild-type x Heterozygote; Heterozygote x Wild-type Coat color: Various Generation: ?+N4F8",
      "detailed_desc": "Dendra2 is a green-to-red, irreversibly photoswitchable monomeric fluorescent protein derived from octocoral Dendronephthya sp.. Its fusion with the mitochondrial targeting signal of subunit VIII of cytochrome c oxidase generates \"mito-Dendra2\", capable of mitochondrial-specific fluorescence. In this PhAMfloxed strain, mito-Dendra2 is knocked-in to the ubiquitously-expressed Gt(ROSA)26Sor gene downstream of a CAG (CMV-&beta;actin) promoter and loxP-flanked Stop sequence to create a conditionally-expressed allele. Matings of floxed homozygous animals have been unproductive in The Jackson Laboratory colony, but heterozygotes can be bred. In the absence of Cre recombinase, no Dendra 2 signal is detected. When exposed to Cre recombinase, either by breeding of the mice with a Cre strain or exposure of cells to viral Cre vectors, selective excision of the floxed termination signal occurs, initiating strong expression of mito-Dendra2. The green fluorescence of mito-Dendra2 co-localizes precisely with mitochondrial marker HSP60 (Hspd1, heat shock protein 1 (chaperonin)). When a sub-population of mitochondria is irradiated with the 405 nm laser light, the green signal photo-converts to red fluorescence, enabling measurements of mitochondrial fusion (indicated by mixing of green and red signals) and transport. When crossed with Meox2 (mesenchyme homeobox 2)-Cre deleter mice, animals homozygous for germline excision of the floxed Stop sequence are viable and fertile (see Stock No. 018397). All organs isolated from these animals (e.g. central nervous system, skeletal muscle, heart, testis, lung, kidney, thymus) exhibit bright fluorescence localized specifically to the mitochondrial compartment. 分子注记：Dendra2 (a green to red irreversibly photoswitchable monomeric fluorescent protein derived from octocoral Dendronephthya sp.) fused to the mitochondrial targeting signal of subunit VIII of cytochrome c oxidase (mito-Dendra2), bovine growth hormone (bGH) polyadenylation signal, and an FRT-flanked neomycin cassette were introduced to Gt(ROSA)26Sor downstream of a CAG (CMV-beta-actin) promoter and loxP-flanked termination signal."
