      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote; Homozygote x Homozygote Generation: N5+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Pik3ca (phosphatidylinositol-4,5-bisphosphate 3-kinase catalytic subunit alpha; also called PI3K) encodes the p110alpha catalytic subunit of phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase. It is one of the most frequently mutated genes in human cancer. H1047R mutations in the kinase domain account for approximately 40% of breast cancer PIK3CA mutant alleles. In this R26-Pik3caH1047R strain, an H1047R mutant form of Pik3ca was targeted to the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus downstream of a floxed STOP cassette. When crossed with an MMTV-Cre strain (see Stock No. 003551 and Stock No. 003553) to excise the floxed stop cassette, Pik3caH1047R is expressed in mammary epithelium. Starting at 5 months of age, females develop mammary tumors as well as lymphoid and skin malignancies. The percentage of animals affected by tumors varied based on the particular MMTV-Cre strain used. Mammary tumors were observed in both virgin and multiparous mice. Males were not studied. R26-Pik3caH1047R mice were also bred to HER2V777L mice, with a Cre-inducible ERBB2 human gene with the activating mutation, V777L, found in breast and colorectal cancer patients. Adenovirus Cre injection into the mammary glands of HER2V777L; PIK3CAH1047R double mutant (HP) mice results in breast cancers with accelerated tumor formation in vivo and increased invasion and migration in in vitro assays. HP breast cancers have resistance to the pan-HER tyrosine kinase inhibitor, neratinib. Of note, this R26-Pik3caH1047R allele is also available on an FVB congenic background as Stock No. 016977. A small percentage of R26-Pik3caH1047R mutant mice show reduced survival on the original FVB congenic background due to development of blood vessel lesions. This has not been detected in this C57BL/6J congenic strain by the donating investigator. 分子注记：The following sequences were inserted into intron 1: splice acceptor site, a STOP cassette (loxP site flanked neomycin resistance gene cassette), Pik3ca cDNA sequence where histidine codon 1047 (CAT) was changed to arginine (p.H1047R), and bovine GH poly(A) signal sequences."
