      "breeding_summary": "Coat color: Agouti Generation: Contact TIS",
      "detailed_desc": "These F1 (first filial generation) hybrid mice are the offspring of a cross between C57BL/6J females (B6) and 129S1/SvImJ males (129S). F1 hybrid mice are heterozygous at all loci (assuming the parental strains have different alleles), and like inbred mice they are genetically and phenotypically uniform. F1 hybrids are often used for hybrid vigor, as a background for some deleterious mutations, for tissue transplantation, to determine the mode of inheritance, to create or enhance expression of polygenic diseases, and to provide physiological buffering (present a broader array of responses to various stresses). B6129 hybrid crosses often provide approximate controls for genetically engineered strains that were generated with 129-derived embryonic stem cells and maintained on a mixed B6;129 background."
