      "detailed_desc": "Mice carrying the MHC class II restricted rearranged T cell receptor transgene, Tg(DO11.10)10Dlo, react to ovalbumin (OVA) peptide antigen. Intraperitoneal administration of OVA to transgenic mice results in a rapid deletion of the immature CD4+ CD8+ TCRlo thymocytes with progression to mature thymocytes. Apoptosis of cortical thymocytes within 20 hours of treatment indicates that apoptosis in important in the development of antigen-induced tolerance. Use of this rearranged T cell receptor transgene requires H2d background.Of note, the DO11 transgene with the C57BL/6-associated Thy1.1 (Thy1a) allele is available as Stock No. 036332 C.Cg-Thy1a Tg(DO11.10)10Dlo/AkhoAbhmJ. 分子注记：This double transgene contains rearranged Tcra and Tcrb genes and is expressed in the majority of T cells. These rearranged transgenes from the DO11.10 T cell hybridoma encode a chicken ovalbumin-specific MHC class II (I-Ad)-restricted T cell receptor. The allele was created by injection of a mix of the two separate transgenes Tg(TcraDO11.10)#Dlo and Tg(TcrbDO11.10)#Dlo into oocytes."
