      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygotes may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN4F2",
      "detailed_desc": "Tfamfl/fl floxed mice possess loxP sites flanking exons 6-7 of the transcription factor A, mitochondrial (Tfam) gene. TFAM is required for the transcription of mitochondrial (mt)DNA encoding electron transport chain subunits. Mice that are homozygous for this allele are viable and fertile. When these mutant mice are bred to mice that express Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have exons 6-7 deleted in cre-expressing tissues. For example, when crossed to B6N.FVB-Tg(ACTB-cre)2Mrt/CjDswJ mice (Stock No. 019099) with widespread expression of Cre recombinase, Tfam+/- mice have 30% to 50% depletion on mtDNA in tissues, with normal amounts of mtDNA transcripts and increased oxidative mtDNA damage. When further crossed to mice susceptible to spontaneous intestinal adenomas, C57BL/6J-ApcMin/J (Stock No. 002020), resulting mice exhibit increased tumor number and growth in the small intestine. 分子注记：A targeting vector was designed to insert a loxP site upstream of exon 6, and a FRT-flanked neomycin resistance (neo) cassette followed by a single loxP site downstream of exon 7 of the gene. Flp mediated recombination removed the neomycin cassette."
