      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, these mice can be bred as homozygotes. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN2F4",
      "detailed_desc": "The L274G point mutation in methionyl-tRNA synthetase 1 results in an altered binding site that enables loading of non-canonical amino-acid methionine analogs, such as azidonorleucine (ANL), onto methionine tRNA. As endogenous wildtype methionyl-tRNA synthetase does not bind ANL, expression of the mutant MetRS (MetRS*) allows the incorporation of ANL into nascent proteins which can then be subsequently labeled by fluorescent non-canonical amino-acid tagging (FUNCAT) or bioorthogonal non-canonical amino acid tagging (BONCAT) for imaging or purification, respectively. STOPflox R26-MetRS* mice were generated by knocking in a floxed STOP cassette, GFP, 2A sequence and mutant Mars1 sequence, all under the control of a CAG promoter, into the endogenous Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. The 2A sequence enables expression of the GFP and mutant Mars1 as discrete translation products from the same single promoter. Following Cre recombinase mediated removal of the floxed STOP cassette, GFP expression and ANL incorporation are only detected in cells expressing the mutant methionine-tRNA synthetase, MetRS* (Mars1*). Mice that are homozygous for the knock-in allele are viable and fertile. When bred to a strain with Cre recombinase expression in CA1 pyramidal cell layer in the hippocampus of the forebrain (see Stock No. 005359 for example), this mutant mouse strain may be useful in studies of nascent proteins and protein synthesis in CA1 pyramidal neurons. Of note, strains containing mutant aminoacyl-tRNA synthetases that recognize azide-bearing noncanonical amino acids include: MetRS* (Stock No. 028071) PheRS* (Stock No. 033734) TyrRS* (Stock No. 033735). 3xMetRS* (Stock No. 040661) is an improved version of STOPflox R26-MetRS* (1xMetRS*; Stock No. 028071) 分子注记：The exchange vector is designed to contain a mutant F3 FRT site, a NEO selection cassette, CAG promoter, a floxed STOP cassette, Green Fluorescent Protein coding sequence, foot-and-mouth disease virus 2A peptide sequence (to mediate ribosomal skipping), the mouse methionine-tRNA synthetase (Mars1) with the L274G point mutation, and an FRT site. This vector was integrated into the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus by recombinase mediated cassette exchange (RMCE). The L274G mutation allows the binding of the methionine surrogate azidonorleucine (ANL) onto the methionine tRNA. ANL can be tagged for imaging or affinity purification."
