      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred together, to wildtype mice from the colony or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Alternatively, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N5+pN2F5",
      "detailed_desc": "The Calb1-IRES2-Cre-D knockin mutation has an IRES2 sequence and a Cre recombinase gene inserted downstream of the translational STOP codon of the calbindin 1 gene (Calb1). As such, Calb1-IRES2-Cre-D mice are designed to have both endogenous gene and Cre recombinase expression directed to calbindin 1-expressing cells by the endogenous promoter/enhancer elements of the Calb1 locus. When Calb1-IRES2-Cre-D mice are bred with mice containing lox-flanked sequences, Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in Calb1-expressing cells in the offspring. The donating investigator reports Cre recombinase expression and activity largely recapitulates the endogenous Calb1 gene's unique expression pattern in many parts of the brain, such as cortex, hippocampus, striatum, thalamus, midbrain and cerebellum. The donating investigator did not examine cre expression in tissues other than brain. Heterozygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. 分子注记：The targeting vector contains, from 5' to 3', an FRT3 site within Calb1 intron 10, a partial Calb1 exon 11 sequence up to and including the endogenous stop codon,an IRES2 sequence, Cre recombinase, a polyA sequence, an AttB site, a PGK-Neomycin cassette, an FRT5 site, an mRNA splice acceptor sequence, the 3' portion of the hygromycin gene (Hygro2) with SV40 late polyA signal, and an AttP site. PhiC31-mediated recombination removed the AttB/AttP-flanked sequence (PGK-Neo-polyA::FRT5::RNA splice acceptor::3'hygro-polyA) and replaced it with the recombined AttB/AttP site (AttL). Mice have both endogenous gene and Cre recombinase expression directed to calbindin 1-expressing cells by the endogenous promoter/enhancer elements of the Calb1 locus."
