      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN3",
      "detailed_desc": "Zbtb46 (zinc finger and BTB domain containing 46; also known as zDC or Btbd4) is a classical dendritic cell (cDC)-restricted zinc finger transcription factor that is not expressed by other immune cell populations, including plasmacytoid dendritic cells, monocytes, or macrophages. It acts primarily as a negative regulator of cDC gene expression. These zDC-Cre mice express IRES-Cre from the 3' UTR of the Zbtb46 (zinc finger and BTB domain containing 46) gene. Expression in classical dendritic cells expressing Zbtb46 has been demonstrated through crosses with floxed stop Gt(ROSA)26Sor-YFP reporter mice. Anecdotal information indicates that female zDC-Cre mice may be more efficient at cre recombinase-mediated excision of loxP-flanked sequences than male zDC-Cre mice. In one study, approximately 95% of offspring derived from crosses of female zDC-Cre mice with floxed allele males carried germline deletions. In contrast, only 5% of the offspring from male zDC-Cre mice carried germline deletions (unpublished; February, 2021). 分子注记：An FRT-flanked neomycin resistance cassette and an IRES-Cre element were introduced to exon 5, immediately after the stop codon. Flp-mediated recombination removed the FRT-flanked neo cassette."
