      "breeding_summary": "The Jackson Laboratory colony shows that homozygous mice of both sexes are viable and fertile (April 2021). Heterozygotes may be bred together, to wildtype littermates or to C57BL/6J (Stock No. 000664). Alternatively, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN2F3",
      "detailed_desc": "The targeted Apoe gene encodes apolipoprotein E, which is important in lipoprotein metabolism and cardiovascular disease as well as Alzheimer's disease, immunoregulation and cognition. CRISPR/Cas9 was used to introduce a C to T nucleotide substitution point mutation in amino acids R130C and R176C into the human APOE sequence in the Apoetm1.1(APOE*4)Adiuj allele. The resulting APOE*2 KI mice express APOE isoform 2, from the endogenous Apoe locus. The APOE 2 isoform is found in approximately 7% of the population, and does not bind to cell surface receptors as well as the 3 and 4 isoforms. As the mice are characterized, we may modify the strain description accordingly. The Jackson Laboratory colony shows that homozygous mice of both sexes are viable and fertile (April 2021). 分子注记：CRISPR/Cas9 genome editing methodologies was used to introduce p.R130C and p.R176C point mutations into human APOE protein carried by the Apoetm1.1(APOE*4)Adpmc allele."
