      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous females may be bred to wildtype (non-carrier) males from the colony, or C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). The donating investigator notes that the Foxg1-IRES-Cre allele should be inherited maternally to ensure the highest and most consistent pattern and levels of Cre activity. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Wild-type Coat color: Black Generation: pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Foxg1-IRES-Cre mice have an IRES-Cre cassette inserted 27 base pairs downstream of the stop codon of the forkhead box G1 (Foxg1) gene. The presence of the IRES-Cre cassette downstream of the stop codon allows for expression of FOXG1 and cre. FOXG1 is involved in the development of the emerging telencephalic region of the brain. Early expression of cre is evident in the telencephalon starting at E8.5-E9.0. Some expression is also observed in other head regions such as the otic vesicle, olfactory placode, anterior half of the optic vesicle, pharyngeal endoderm, and also fore gut by E10.5. Homozygous mice are viable and fertile. When these mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequence, Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the Cre-expressing cells of the offspring. The donating investigator notes that the Foxg1-IRES-Cre allele should be inherited maternally to ensure the highest and most consistent pattern and levels of Cre activity. In contrast to the Foxg1-Cre knock-in/knock-out strains (Stock Nos. 006084 and 004337), this Foxg1-IRES-Cre strain coexpresses FOXG1 and Cre recombinase, preventing Foxg1-haploinsufficiency and ectopic cre expression. If the recombinase activity pattern of this allele is further characterized by the Genetic Resource Science group at The Jackson Laboratory, such findings will be reported on the Mouse Genome Informatics (MGI) Allele Detail entry. This same information may also be found searching the MGI Recombinase Activity and MGI Gene Expression + Recombinase Activity Comparison Matrix. 分子注记：An IRES-cre gene followed by an frt-flanked PGK-neo was inserted at 27bp downstream of the stop codon of the gene by homologous recombination in ES cells. Resulting mice were crossed with FLPe expressing mice to remove the PGK-neo cassette."
