      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred together, to wildtype mice from the colony or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Alternatively, homozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities - and homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Wild-type x Heterozygote; Heterozygote x Wild-type Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "The adenylate cyclase activating polypeptide 1 protein (ADCYAP1 or PACAP) encoded by the Adcyap1 gene is a neuropeptide/neurotrophin that functions as a hypophysiotropic hormone, neurotransmitter and neuromodulator, and also plays a role in paracrine and autocrine regulation of certain cell types. In addition, warm-sensitive neurons within the preoptic hypothalamus that coordinate the diverse behavioral and autonomic responses to heat are molecularly defined by co-expression of the neuropeptides BDNF and ADCYAP1. The Adcyap1-2A-Cre knock-in mutation has a F2A sequence and Cre recombinase gene inserted inserted immediately upstream of the Adcyap1 translational STOP codon - this is designed to have the endogenous promoter/enhancer elements directing cre expression to ADCYAP1+ cells. When Adcyap1-2A-Cre mice are bred with mice containing lox-flanked sequences, Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in Adcyap1-expressing cells in the offspring. The donating investigators report Cre recombinase expression and activity recapitulates the endogenous Adcyap1 gene in adult mice. Expression is observed in preoptic hypothalamus of adult mice. Additionally, expression is enriched in restricted populations within the olfactory areas, hippocampus, striatum, thalamus, midbrain, pons and medulla, and scattered within the isocortex and hypothalamus. Importantly, the donating investigators report that Adcyap expression during development results in widespread recombination of floxed conditional alleles integrated into the genome (e.g., Gt(ROSA)26Sor reporters) - and they suggest genetic access to ADCYAP1+ cells in adult brain may benefit by using Cre-dependent AAV injections. The donating investigators did not examine cre expression in tissues other than brain. This knock-in allele is designed to avoid disrupting expression of the endogenous protein; although Adcyap1 expression from the Adcyap1-2A-Cre allele has not been evaluated to date (February 2017). Homozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. For original characterization information, see images at the Allen Institute for Brain Science website (Adcyap1-2A-Cre images). 分子注记：The targeting vector contains from 5' to 3', a partial Adcyap1 sequence spanning intron 1 through part of exon 5 (with an FRT3 site in intron 4) up to but not including the endogenous stop codon, a viral 2A oligopeptide sequence (F2A; mediates ribosomal skippi"
