      "detailed_desc": "The Esr2 gene encodes the DNA binding central C domain of estrogen receptor beta (ER-&beta;). ESR2 is one of two estrogen receptors, a ligand-activated transcription factor and nuclear hormone receptor. ESR2 is normally expressed in many tissues including uterus, blood monocytes, tissue macrophages, and colonic, pulmonary and prostate epithelial cells, as well as in malignant counterparts of these tissues. In addition, ESR2 is found throughout the brain at different concentrations in different neuron clusters. The Esr2-IRES2-Cre-D knock-in mutation has an IRES2 sequence and a Cre recombinase gene inserted downstream of the Esr2 translational STOP codon - this is designed to have the endogenous promoter/enhancer elements direct cre expression to ESR2+ cells. When Esr2-IRES2-Cre-D mice are bred with mice containing lox-flanked sequences, Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in Esr2-expressing cells in the offspring. The donating investigator reports Cre recombinase expression/activity largely recapitulates the endogenous Esr2 gene expression in the brain - observed mainly in medial amygdalar nucleus, bed nuclei of the stria terminalis, paraventricular hypothalamic nucleus, cortical layer 6 and scattered neurons elsewhere in the brain. They did not examine cre expression in tissues other than brain. This knock-in allele is designed to avoid disrupting expression of the endogenous protein; although Esr2 expression from the Esr2-IRES2-Cre-D allele has not been evaluated to date (March 2017). Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. To date (March 2017), it has not been attempted to make this strain homozygous. 分子注记：The targeting vector contained, from 5' to 3', a partial Esr2 sequence spanning exon 10 (including the endogenous stop codon), an internal ribosome entry site 2 (IRES2) sequence (allows translation initiation in the middle of an mRNA sequence), a Cre recombinase gene, a bovine growth hormone polyA sequence, an AttB site, a PGK promoter-Neomycin resistance gene-PGK polyA cassette, an frt5 site, an mRNA splice acceptor sequence, the 3' portion of the hygromycin gene (Hygro2) with SV40 polyA signal, and an AttP site. PhiC31-mediated recombination removed the AttB/AttP-flanked sequence (PGK-Neo-polyA::FRT5::RNA splice acceptor::3'hygro-polyA) and replaced it with the recombined AttB/AttP site (AttL). The resulting Esr2-IRES2-Cre-D mice were bred with C57BL/"
