      "breeding_summary": "The Jackson Laboratory has determined homozygous mice are viable and fertile (March 2024) and will maintain our live colony by breeding homozygous mice together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N5+pN2F7",
      "detailed_desc": "The Npy gene encodes neuropeptide Y (NPY) - a 36-amino acid neurotransmitter expressed in subsets of interneurons in the brain. Upon association with its target receptors (e.g., G protein-coupled receptors), NPY functions in neurobiology (behavioral and molecular processes), energy metabolism, obesity, seizures and epilepsy. The Npy-IRES2-FlpO-D knock-in mutation has an IRES2 sequence and an optimized FLP recombinase (FlpO) gene inserted downstream of the Npy translational STOP codon - this is designed to have the endogenous promoter/enhancer elements direct FlpO expression to NPY+ cells. When Npy-IRES2-FlpO-D mice are bred with mice containing frt-flanked sequences, FlpO-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the frt-flanked sequences in Npy-expressing cells in the offspring. The donating investigator reports FlpO recombinase expression/activity largely recapitulates the endogenous Npy gene - observed mainly in cortex, hippocampus, striatum and suprachiasmatic nucleus, as well as in scattered neurons elsewhere in the brain. The donating investigator did not examine FlpO expression in tissues other than brain. This knock-in allele is designed to avoid disrupting expression of the endogenous protein; although Npy expression from the Npy-IRES2-FlpO-D allele has not been evaluated to date (March 2017). Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. The Jackson Laboratory has determined homozygous mice are viable and fertile (March 2024). 分子注记：The targeting vector contains, from 5' to 3', a partial Npy sequence spanning exon 4 (including the endogenous stop codon), an internal ribosome entry site 2 sequence, a FlpO recombinase gene (a codon-optimized FLPe gene modified for translation in mammalian cells and higher recombination efficiency in cells and in mice), a bovine growth hormone polyA sequence, an AttB site, a PGK promoter-Neomycin resistance gene-PGK polyA cassette, an frt5 site, an mRNA splice acceptor sequence, the 3' portion of the hygromycin gene (Hygro2) with SV40 polyA signal, and an AttP site. PhiC31-mediated recombination removed the AttB/AttP-flanked sequence (PGK-Neo-polyA::frt5::RNA splice acceptor::3'hygro-polyA) and replaced it with the recombined AttB/AttP site (AttL)."
