      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred to wildtype mice from the colony or to C57BL/6NJ inbred mice (Stock No. 005304). Alternatively, homozygous mice are viable and fertile, and may be bred together. The Jackson Laboratory colony of this strain initially incorporated animals that were black or albino. While no phenotypic differences associated with coat color have been noted here by our colony managers, a decision was made to breed out the albino allele for uniformity (March, 2023).&nbsp; Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN2F5pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "The Fos2A-iCreER knock-in allele (also called Fos2A-iCreERT2 or \"TRAP2\") was designed to have expression of a tamoxifen-inducible, improved Cre recombinase (iCreERT2) from the Fos promoter/enhancer elements - without disrupting endogenous Fos expression. The donating investigator reports this allele preserves endogenous Fos, including the highly conserved first intron and the 3' untranslated region critical for mRNA destabilization. [DeNardo et al. 2019 Nat Neurosci. 22:460] iCreERT2 fusion protein activity is inducible; observed following tamoxifen administration. When Fos2A-iCreER mice are bred with mice containing lox-flanked sequences, tamoxifen-inducible iCre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of floxed sequences in the Fos-expressing cells of the offspring. Specifically, the donating investigator reports that following tamoxifen induction, Cre recombinase activity is observed in active populations of neurons in the brain - in a pattern consistent with endogenous Fos expression. Before tamoxifen exposure, some Cre recombination/activity is reported in the olfactory bulb - but those baseline levels are significantly less than the tamoxifen-induced levels of Cre recombination/activity. The donating investigator did not examine iCreERT2 expression in tissues other than brain. Prior to tamoxifen exposure, heterozygous Fos2A-iCreER mice are viable and fertile with no behavioral, neurological or any other spontaneous abnormalities. Additionally, the Fos2A-iCreER colony at The Jackson Laboratory is viable and fertile as homozygotes. The iCreERT2 fusion protein used here consists of a codon-improved Cre recombinase fused to a G400V/M543A/L544A triple mutant form of the human estrogen receptor which does not bind its natural ligand (17&beta;-estradiol) at physiological concentrations but will bind the synthetic estrogen receptor ligands 4-hydroxytamoxifen (OHT or tamoxifen) and, with lesser sensitivity, ICI 182780. Restricted to the cytoplasm, iCre/ERT2 can only gain access to the nuclear compartment after exposure to tamoxifen. To counteract the mixed estrogen agonist effects of tamoxifen injections, which can result in late fetal abortions in pregnant mice, progesterone may be coadministered. 分子注记：A targeting vector was designed to insert a 2A::iCreER::frt-neo-frt cassette into the translational stop site of the FBJ osteosarcoma oncogene locus (Fos) on chromosome 12. The viral 2A oligopeptide sequence mediates ribosomal skipping. The iCreER fusio"
