      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, these mice can be bred as double homozygotes. Coat color: Various Generation: ?+pN1F21",
      "detailed_desc": "The targeted Wwtr1 gene (also known as TAZ) encodes a transcriptional coactivator that with YAP, encoded by the Yap1 gene, are downstream effectors of the Hippo pathway. YAP/WWTR1 are involved in the regulation of cell proliferation, differentiation, and survival as well as mechanotransduction, epithelial-mesenchymal transition in the extracellular matrix, organ size, and stem cell self-renewal. When YAP/WWTR1 are translocated to the nucleus (inactivated Hippo signaling), they act as coactivators for TEA domain (TEAD) transcription factors. Dysregulated Hippo signaling has been associated with a number of human cancers. Mutations in the Yap1 gene have been associated with ocular coloboma, with or without hearing impairment, cleft lip/palate, and/or mental retardation. These double floxed mice possess loxP sites on either side of exon 2 of the targeted Wwtr1 gene and loxP sites on either side of exon 2 of the targeted Yap1 gene. Mice that are homozygous for both of these alleles are viable and fertile. When these mutant mice are bred to mice that express Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have exon 2 of Wwtr1 and exon 2 of Yap1 deleted in the cre-expressing tissues. Removal of the floxed sequence creates null alleles. When bred to a strain with Cre recombinase expression in nephron progenitor cells, this mutant mouse strain may be useful in studies of kidney organogenesis. When bred to a strain with Cre recombinase expression in Schwann cells (see Stock No. 017927 for example), this mutant mouse strain may be useful in studies of myelination and axonal sorting during neuronal development. When bred to a strain with Cre recombinase expression in villus and crypt epithelial cells of the small and large intestines (see Stock No. 021504 for example), this mutant mouse strain may be useful in studies of intestinal adenoma and tumor suppression. 分子注记：An FRT flanked splice acceptor-IRES-betageo cassette and loxP site were inserted in intron 1 and a loxP site was inserted in intron 2 via homologous recombination. Breeding to Flpe-expressing mice removed the FRT-flanked SA-IRES-betageo. A loxP site was inserted in intron 1 and a loxP site and FRT-flanked neo cassette were inserted in intron 2 via homologous recombination. Breeding to Flpe-expressing mice removed the FRT-flanked NEO."
