      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, hemizygous mice may be bred together. The donating lab has not attempted to make this strain homozygous. Mating scheme: Noncarrier x Hemizygote; Hemizygote x Noncarrier Coat color: Black Generation: N7+N1pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Tie2-CreERT2 mice express a tamoxifen-inducible codon improved Cre recombinase gene under direction of the TEK receptor tyrosine kinase (Tek) promoter on a BAC transgene. These mice express Cre-ERT2 protein in endothelial cells. Restricted to the cytoplasm, Cre-ERT2 can only gain access to the nuclear compartment after exposure to tamoxifen. When these mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequence, tamoxifen-inducible, cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the cre-expressing endothelial cells of the offspring. Mice hemizygous for the Tie2-CreERT2 transgene are viable and fertile. The donating lab has not attempted to make this strain homozygous. For other strains expressing Cre recombinase in endothelial cells under direction of the Tek promoter see Stock No. 004128 and Stock No. 008863. 分子注记：A tamoxifen-inducible icre recombinase gene and FRT-flanked beta-lactamase gene were inserted into the ATG start site of the murine Tek gene located on a BAC. After Flpe-mediated excision of the beta-lactamase gene, the targeted BAC was injected into FVB/N oocytes. Cre expression was detected in endothelial cells of numerous organs after treatment with tamoxifen."
