      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred together, to wildtype mice from the colony or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). To date (January 2018), it has not been attempted to make this strain homozygous. Mating scheme: Wild-type x Heterozygote; Heterozygote x Wild-type Coat color: Black Generation: N11+pN3F2",
      "detailed_desc": "The Oxtr gene encodes the oxytocin receptor. Oxtr polymorphisms are of interest in studying human psychology behavioral phenotypes (e.g., autism spectrum disorder). The Oxtr-T2A-Cre-D knock-in mutation has a T2A sequence and a Cre recombinase gene inserted immediately at the Oxtr translational STOP codon - this is designed to have the endogenous promoter/enhancer elements direct cre expression to OXTR+ cells. When Oxtr-T2A-Cre-D mice are bred with mice containing lox-flanked sequences, Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in Oxtr-expressing cells in the offspring. The donating investigator reports Cre recombinase expression/activity largely recapitulates the endogenous Oxtr gene expression in the brain. Specifically, Cre is enriched in restricted populations within the hippocampal formation, cortical subplate, striatum, thalamus, hypothalamus and medulla. Sparse, scattered expression is present in the cortex. They did not examine cre expression in tissues other than brain. This knock-in allele is designed to avoid disrupting expression of the endogenous protein; although Oxtr expression from the Oxtr-T2A-Cre-D allele has not been evaluated to date (January 2018). Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. To date (January 2018), it has not been attempted to make this strain homozygous. For characterization information, see images at the Allen Institute for Brain Science website (Oxtr-T2A-Cre-D images). 分子注记：The targeting vector contained, from 5' to 3', a partial Oxtr sequence spanning intron 1 up to but not including the endogenous stop codon in exon 2 (with a frt3 site in intron 1), a viral 2A oligopeptide sequence (T2A; mediates ribosomal skipping), a Cre recombinase gene, a bovine growth hormone polyA sequence, an AttB site, a PGK/gb2 promoter-Neomycin resistance gene-PGK polyA cassette, a frt5 site, an mRNA splice acceptor sequence, the 3' portion of the hygromycin gene (Hygro2) with SV40 polyA signal, and an AttP site. PhiC31-mediated recombination removed the AttB/AttP-flanked sequences (PGK/gb2-Neo-pA::frt5::RNA splice acceptor::3'hygro-pA) and replace it with the recombined AttB/AttP site (AttL)."
