      "breeding_summary": "Tlr7 is X-linked. When maintaining a live colony, homozygous females may be bred to hemizyous males. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Hemizygote Coat color: Black Generation: N?+pN1F1pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "TLR7KI knock-in mice have a FLAG tag and an IRES-tdTomato sequence placed at the 3' end of the X-linked toll-like receptor 7 (Tlr7) gene. TLR7 is a cell-surface receptor which plays a fundamental role in pathogen recognition and activation of innate immunity. This gene has been implicated in the pathogenesis of several autoimmune diseases including inflammatory bowel disease and Crohn's Disease, as well as some intestinal cancers. In these mice, tdTomato is expressed in splenic CD11c+ dendritic cells (DCs). Extremely low tdTomato levels are evident in intestinal epithelial cells (IECs) throughout the small intestine and the proximal colon, with similar expression seen in neonates as seen in adults. tdTomato can be detected by using FACS analysis or immunohistochemistry. Homozygous females and hemizygous males are viable and fertile. Of note, similar TLR reporter mice are available: TLR2KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031822) contain an HA tag and an IRES-EGFP sequence. TLR4KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031824) contain an HA tag and an IRES-EYFP sequence. TLR5KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031825) contain an HA tag and an IRES-tdTomato sequence. TLR9KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031829) contain an HA tag and an IRES-EGFP sequence. 分子注记：A FLAG tag was fused to the 3' end of the gene followed by an IRES-tdTomato reporter via homologous recombination. The vector also contained a loxP-flanked neomycin selection (neo) cassette, which was removed following Cre-mediated recombination."
