      "detailed_desc": "TLR9KI knock-in mice have a hemagglutinin (HA) tag and an IRES-EGFP sequence placed at the 3' end of the toll-like receptor 9 (Tlr9) gene. TLR9 is a cell-surface receptor which plays a fundamental role in recognizing DNA that contains unmethylated CpG dinucleotides, and subsequent activation of innate immunity. This gene has been implicated in the pathogenesis of several autoimmune diseases including inflammatory bowel disease and Crohn's Disease, as well as some intestinal cancers. In these mice, EGFP is expressed in splenic CD11c+ dendritic cells (DCs). Extremely low EGFP levels are evident in intestinal epithelial cells (IECs) throughout the small intestine and the proximal colons with similar expression seen in neonates as seen in adults. EGFP can be detected by using FACS analysis or immunohistochemistry. Homozygotes are viable and fertile. Of note, similar TLR reporter mice are available: TLR2KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031822) contain an HA tag and an IRES-EGFP sequence. TLR4KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031824) contain an HA tag and an IRES-EYFP sequence. TLR5KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031825) contain an HA tag and an IRES-tdTomato sequence. TLR7KI knock-in mice (Stock No. 031827) contain a FLAG tag and an IRES-tdTomato sequence. 分子注记：An HA tag was fused to the 3' end of the gene followed by an IRES-GFP reporter via homologous recombination. The vector also contained a loxP-flanked neomycin selection (neo) cassette, which was removed by Cre-mediated recombination."
