      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, these mice can be bred as homozygotes. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN3F3",
      "detailed_desc": "These LSL-Salsa6f transgenic reporter mice carry the Gt(ROSA)26SorpCAG-FRT-LSL-Salsa6f-WPRE-bGHpA-AttB/P allele designed with a floxed-STOP cassette upstream of the Salsa6f ratiometric fusion calcium indicator (tdTomato linked to GCaMP6f by a V5 epitope tag). Although under control of the endogenous Gt(ROSA)26Sor promoter/enhancer regions and the CAG hybrid promoter, widespread expression of Salsa6f is prevented by a STOP cassette. Red fluorescence is observed following exposure to Cre recombinase, and green fluorescence is detected following calcium binding. The ratio of red and green fluorescence allows monitoring of the intracellular concentration of calcium ions in vivo. Mice that are homozygous for the targeted mutation are viable and fertile. When bred to a strain with Cre recombinase expression in CD4+ T cells (see Stock No. 017336 for example), this mutant mouse strain may be useful in studies monitoring cytosolic calcium signaling (single-cell ratiometric calcium ion) during T cell receptor activation. The resulting Cre-recombined mice that are homozygous for the Salsa6f allele exhibited a two-fold increase in tdTomato (red) fluorescence compared to mice heterozygous for the Salsa6f allele. Expression of Salsa6f does not alter T lymphocyte development or function. Salsa6f expression is predominately localized to the cytosol, facilitating tracking of cells in the absence of calcium signaling, enable ratiometric calcium imaging to eliminate motility artifacts, and permit convenient single-wavelength femtosecond excitation for two-photon microscopy. 分子注记：The targeting vector contains (5' to 3'): CAG (cytomegalovirus early enhancer/chicken beta-actin) promoter, an FRT site, loxP-STOP-loxP cassette, Salsa6f (see below), WPRE, bGHpA, AttB site, an FRT site, neomycin selection cassette, AttP site (using the Addgene Plasmid #34883); inserted into the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. PhiC31-mediated recombination removed the AttB/AttP-flanked sequence. Salsa6f contains tdTomato linked to GCaMP6f by a V5 epitope tag."
