      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, hemizygous mice may be bred together. The donating lab has not attempted to make a homozygous colony. Mating scheme: Noncarrier x Hemizygote; Hemizygote x Noncarrier Coat color: Black Generation: N1+N1pN1F1",
      "detailed_desc": "The mito::mKate2 transgenic mice have the ubiquitous CAG promoter directing expression of a far-red fluorescent protein (mKate2) with N-terminal fusion of the cytochrome c oxidase subunit VIII mitochondrial targeting signal, resulting in direct fluorescence in the mitochondria. mKate2 mice can be used for in vivo and ex vivo imaging of mitochondria within living tissues. Fluorescence is detected in the tissues tested, specifically, adult flexor digitorum brevis (FDB) muscle, sperm midpiece, Purkinje neurons of the cerebellum, retina, heart, and liver. mito::mKate2 are useful for monitoring mitochondrial dynamics coincident with cell cycle kinetics during mouse embryonic development and in adult tissues. mKate2 can be visualized with other traditional fluorescent reporters (such as GFP, YFP, CFP, and DsRed) since its fluorescence lies outside of the blue/green/red color range. Hemizygous mice are viable and fertile, the donating lab has not attempted to make a homozygous colony. 分子注记：The transgene is composed of an N-terminal mitochondrial targeting pre-sequence (derived from human cytochrome c oxidase subunit VIII [COX8A]), fused to a far-red fluorescent protein, mKate2. The fusion protein cDNA sequence was placed downstream of the CMV enhancer/chicken beta-actin (CAG) promoter."
