      "breeding_summary": "Prior to Cre recombinase exposure, heterozygous mice (Dnmt3afl-R878H/+) are viable and fertile, with normal breeding, normal expression of endogenous DNMT3A, and no gross phenotype or behavioral abnormalities. Homozygous mice often exhibit dermatitis with onset 2-4 months of age (December 2019). Therefore, when maintaining a live colony at The Jackson Laboratory, heterozygous mice are bred to wildtype mice from the colony or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Mating scheme: Wild-type x Heterozygote; Heterozygote x Wild-type Generation: ?+pN2pN1F2",
      "detailed_desc": "DNA methyltransferase 3a (DNMT3A) mutations are commonly associated with aging-associated clonal hematopoiesis, acute myeloid leukemia (AML) and other hematological malignancies. In humans, the majority of mutations are heterozygous point mutations within the catalytic domain at DNMT3A residue R882 (equivalent to R878 in mouse), which is proposed to induce a dominant-negative loss of de novo methylation activity. Dnmt3afl-R878H mice have loxP-flanked Dnmt3a exon 23 and polyA STOP sequences followed by a modified Dnmt3a exon 23 sequence encoding the R878H mutation. The Dnmt3afl-R878H allele is designed to express endogenous DNMT3A prior to Cre recombinase exposure, and then express the mutant protein DNMT3A*R878H after exposure to Cre recombinase. Prior to Cre recombinase exposure, heterozygous mice (Dnmt3afl-R878H/+) are viable and fertile, with normal breeding, normal expression of endogenous DNMT3A, and no gross phenotype or behavioral abnormalities. Homozygous mice often exhibit dermatitis with onset 2-4 months of age (December 2019). The homozygous phenotype has not been further characterized (December 2019). Upon exposure to Cre recombinase, the loxP-flanked endogenous exon 23 is deleted and replaced with the R878H mutant exon 23 (that retains the endogenous polyA and 3' UTR elements) - resulting in expression of the DNMT3A*R878H mutant protein. For example, when Dnmt3afl-R878H are bred to Mx1-Cre transgenic mice (Stock No. 003556), the resulting Dnmt3afl-R878H/+ Mx1-Cre animals exhibit no observable change in frequency of hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells in the bone marrow prior to injection of interferon alpha, interferon beta or synthetic double-stranded RNA (such as poly I:C). Upon poly I:C injection, Dnmt3afl-R878H/+ Mx1-Cre animals exhibit heterozygous expression of DNMT3A*R878H (mimicking the condition most commonly observed in human) - resulting in expansion of hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells consistent with a clonal hematopoiesis phenotype. In addition to these Dnmt3afl-R878H mice (Stock No. 032289), The Jackson Laboratory Repository also has available Stock No. 031514 (Dnmt3aR878H). While both mouse lines allow Cre recombinase-inducible DNMT3A*R878H expression, they differ in that Dnmt3afl-R878H (Stock No. 032289) has endogenous DNMT3A expression before Cre exposure, whereas Stock No. 031514 does not express endogenous exon 23 before Cre exposure. 分子注记：The targeting vector was designed to insert a loxP site, a PGK-Puro selecti"
