      "breeding_summary": "Hemizygotes and homozygotes retaining the floxed-STOP cassette are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN3F5",
      "detailed_desc": "Mitochondria serve to generate large quantities of cellular energy in the form of adenosine triphosphate (ATP), and perform a number of other functions within eukaryotic cells. Much remains to be learned about their diverse morphologies and mechanisms, however. Cre recombinase-mediated excision of a loxP-flanked STOP cassette in these MITO-Tag mice enables cell-type-specific expression of hemagglutinin (HA)-tagged EGFP that localizes on the outer membranes of mitochondria. These features enable immunocapture of mitochondria from specific cell types. Mice retaining the floxed-STOP cassette exhibit no overt phenotype. 分子注记：The targeting construct containing (from 5' t 3') CAG-loxP-neomycin (reversed)-pA-loxP-3xHA-EGFP-SYNJ2BP-lacZ-BGH-pA is targeted to intron 1 of the gene. The 3xHA-EGFP-SYNJ2BP components constitute the \"MITO-Tag\" cassette targeting the 3XHA epitope tag with GFP to the mitochondrial membrane. The construct includes only the transmembrane domain of the rat Synj2bp/OMP25 (AA109-145) gene. The small fragment of lacZ incorporated in the mutation is not expected to be functional."
