      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN2pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Cardiac cells expressing Ly6a (lymphocyte antigen 6 complex, locus A; also called Sca1) predominantly contribute to the cardiac vasculature, particularly in the endothelial cell expansion and remodeling that occurs early after birth or following myocardial infarction (MI). These Ly6aMerCreMer knock-in/knock-out mice express tamoxifen-inducible cre recombinase (MerCreMer) from the mouse Ly6a promoter in tissues that normally express the Ly6a gene. Expression of Ly6a is eliminated in the targeted allele. Tamoxifen-inducible expression of a cre-dependent eGFP reporter has been confirmed by immunohistochemistry in heart and kidney tissues. Crosses with cre-responsive R26-eGFP reporter mice (generated through a cross of R26-NZG (Stock No. 012429) with Pgk1-FLPo (Stock No. 011065)) coincident with tamoxifen administration enable permanent labeling and lineage tracing of cells that normally express Ly6a throughout development and postnatal growth, or after cardiac injury. Progeny of this cross that are treated with tamoxifen throughout adulthood (starting at 3 months of age) show endothelial cell labeling across multiple tissues examined (heart, lung, liver, intestine, kidney, spleen) in addition to other hepatic cells, parenchymal cells of the kidney, and splenocytes. 分子注记：A cDNA encoding a MerCreMer fusion protein and an FRT-flanked neomycin cassette were recombined in-frame with the Ly6a ATG start codon (exon 2) via homologous recombination in embryonic stem (ES) cells. The MerCreMer double fusion protein incorporates a cre recombinase cDNA sequence flanked by mutated murine estrogen receptor (mer) ligand binding domains (amino acids 281-599, G525R). Resultant mice were crossed with Flpe mice to delete the neomycin cassette. Expression of Ly6a is eliminated in the targeted allele."
