      "detailed_desc": "MitoTag (Rosa26-CAG-LSL-GFP-OMM) is a Gt(ROSA)26Sor knock-in allele that has a loxP-flanked STOP cassette preventing transcription of an outer mitochondrial membrane-targeted enhanced green fluorescent protein (GFP-OMM). These mice are designed to allow Cre recombinase-inducible EGFP fluorescence that faithfully localizes to mitochondria (with no observed cytosolic fluorescence). Prior to Cre recombinase exposure, the donating investigator reports the floxed-STOP cassette prevents expression of GFP-OMM. Both heterozygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile with normal breeding, and no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. Following Cre recombinase exposure, deletion of the STOP cassette allows GFP-OMM to be expressed - resulting in outer mitochondrial membrane-tagged EGFP fluorescence that can be robust and bright. Specifically, the donating investigator reports GFP-OMM faithfully localizes to mitochondria (with no observed cytosolic fluorescence) in all Cre recombinase-expressing lines they tested, including GFAP-Cre line 77.6 (astrocytes; Stock No. 024098), L7-Cre (Purkinje cells; Stock No. 004146), Emx1-Cre (forebrain neural cells; Stock No. 005628), ChAT-Cre (cholinergic neurons; Stock No. 006410), Cx3cr1CreER (monocytes/macrophages; Stock No. 020940), LysMcre (myeloid cell lineage; Stock No. 004781), PLP/creERT (oligodendrocytes/Schwann cells; Stock No. 005975), Pvalb-T2A-Cre-D (scattered interneuron populations; Stock No. 012358), TRPV1Cre (dorsal root ganglia, peripheral sensory nerve endings and CNS; Stock No. 017769), Sst-IRES-Cre (dendritic inhibitory interneurons; Stock No. 018973), Vip-IRES-cre (GABAergic interneurons; Stock No. 010908) and CAGGCre-ERTM (widespread cells; Stock No. 004682). In addition, double mutant ChAT-Cre;GFP-OMM mice exhibited no adverse effects on mitochondrial or cellular health in motor neurons (i.e., normal mitochondrial transport and shape, as well as neuromuscular synapse morphology). The Jackson Laboratory Repository has several lines with Cre recombinase-inducible mitochondrial fluorescence, including Dr. Thomas Misgeld's MitoTag (Rosa26-CAG-LSL-GFP-OMM) (Stock No. 032675 ; Rosa26::PGK::attL::neo::CAG::loxP-STOP-loxP::GFP-OMM::attR), Dr. David Sabatini's MITO-Tag (Stock No. 032290 ; Rosa26::CAG::loxP-STOP-loxP::3xHA-EGFP-SYNJ2BP::lacZ::BGH-pA) and Dr. Jeremy Nathans' ROSA-MitoGFP (Stock No. 021429 ; Rosa26::CAG::loxP-STOP-loxP::MitoGFP-3xV5::BGH::frt-PGK-neo-frt). While both the MitoTag (Rosa2"
