      "breeding_summary": "Compound heterozygous (HET/HET) breedings are recommended for this strain. Compound homozygous&nbsp;(HOM/HOM) females are not good mothers as the antibodies they produce react to molecules in the brain of pups, resulting in death during development. They also become very sick around 1 year of age.&nbsp; HOM/HOM males survive better (sometimes up to 2 years), but develop cognitive disorders. Females homozygous for the Igh allele are less productive that females homozygous for the Igk allele.&nbsp; Females homozygous for the Igh allele deliver fewer (or no) female pups. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Generation: N10pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE) is characterized by the production of autoantibodies that are frequently directed against nucleic acid-associated antigens. This 564Igi model system incorporates heavy and light chain genes encoding 564 immunoglobulin (derived from an autoimmune SWRxNZB hybridoma) targeted to the heavy and light chain loci in non-autoimmune C57BL/6 background mice.The antibody recognizes RNA, single-stranded DNA, and nucleosomes. B cells expressing this immunoglobulin are activated, producing class-switched autoantibody in vivo despite an apparently normal induction of anergy. Production of these autoantibodies is sufficient to cause kidney pathology, as determined by immunofluorescent staining, and electron/light microscopy of frozen kidney sections taken from 13-month-old animals. Compound heterozygous (HET/HET) breedings are recommended for this strain. Compound homozygous&nbsp;(HOM/HOM) females are not good mothers as the antibodies they produce react to molecules in the brain of pups, resulting in death during development. They also become very sick around 1 year of age.&nbsp; HOM/HOM males survive better (sometimes up to 2 years), but develop cognitive disorders. 分子注记：A floxed neomycin resistance gene, as well as the 564 VkappaJkappa5 region from a hybridoma derived from an autoimmune SWRxNZB mouse, replaced a segment of DNA including the entire J kappa region. Male chimeric mice were bred to C57BL/6 females. Offspring from these mice were crossed with cre expressing transgenic mice in order to excise the neomycin resistance cassette. A floxed neomycin resistance gene, as well as the VDJ 564 region from a hybridoma derived from an autoimmune SWRxNZB mouse, replaced a segment of DNA including DQ52 and the entire JH region."
