      "breeding_summary": "Hemizygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Noncarrier x Hemizygote; Hemizygote x Noncarrier Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Acta2 (actin alpha 2, smooth muscle, aorta or &alpha;SMA) encodes a smooth muscle actin expressed in a population of mesenchymal progenitor cells located in perivascular niches, the periosteum and sutures. This population of cells plays a role in bone remodeling and regeneration. &alpha;SMACreERT2 transgenic mice contain a mouse Acta2 promoter directing tamoxifen-inducible Cre recombinase expression. When transgenic mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked (floxed) sequences, tamoxifen-inducible cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of floxed sequences in &alpha;SMA-expressing cells in the offspring. Hemizygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported phenotype abnormalities. Double mutant &alpha;SMACreERT2 and Gt(ROSA)26Sortm9(CAG-tdTomato)Hze (Ai9; Stock No. 007909) mice administered tamoxifen have SMA9+ cells detected in the primary spongiosa or the periosteum, but not within the bone matrix. No leaky expression of tdTomato is detected in bone tissue, however, cre expression is observed in tissues with strong &alpha;SMA expression like bladder and aorta. 17 days following tamoxifen administration tdTomato labeling identifies multiple osteoblasts and osteocytes. This strain may be useful in lineage tracing studies of bone remodeling and regeneration. Outside of bone tdTomato expression is observed in perivascular cells within various tissues (skin, liver, kidney, lungs) and in myoepithelial cells with progenitor characteristics within the mammary glands and olfactory glands. The Cre-ERT2 fusion protein consists of Cre recombinase fused to a triple mutant form of the human estrogen receptor which does not bind its natural ligand (17&beta;-estradiol) at physiological concentrations but will bind the synthetic estrogen receptor ligands 4-hydroxytamoxifen (OHT or tamoxifen) and, with lesser sensitivity, ICI 182780. Restricted to the cytoplasm, Cre-ERT2 can only gain access to the nuclear compartment after exposure to tamoxifen. To counteract the mixed estrogen agonist effects of tamoxifen injections, which can result in late fetal abortions in pregnant mice, progesterone may be coadministered. 分子注记：The cre/ERT2 cDNA and BGH polyA cDNAs was inserted into a construct containing the vascular smooth muscle alpha-actin (Acta2) promoter. Functionality of the construct to modify floxed reporter constructs was tested by transient transfection of smooth muscle cell cultures. The purified vector was injected into fertilized C57BL"
