      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N12+pN2F3",
      "detailed_desc": "Neurons that express Calca (calcitonin/calcitonin-related polypeptide, alpha) within the parabrachial nuclear region of the brain form a functionally important circuit affecting appetite. Activation of these neurons projecting to the central nucleus of the amygdala suppresses appetite. These neurons are activated by a wide variety of real threats, potential threats and cues associated with threats (PMID 29562230 and 30344042) These CalcaCre knock-in/knock-out targeted mutant mice express Myc-tagged, nuclear-localized cre recombinase:EGFP fusion protein targeted to the first coding exon of the mouse Calca gene. Crosses of this strain with a reporter line (e.g. Ai14, Stock No. 007914) reveal widespread expression in the brain during development. Expression is restricted in adults (similar to in situ results shown in Allen Brain Atlas). Cre-dependent adeno-associated virus (AAV) carrying an mCherry reporter delivered directly into the parabrachial nucleus (PBN) region of adult CalcaCre mice results in specific expression of mCherry in CGRP (calcitonin gene-related peptide)-positive neurons in the PBelo (outer external lateral subdivision of the PBN).Heterozygotes demonstrate no overt phenotype. Homozygotes have no (or greatly reduced) expression of CALCA and CGRP and presumably have mild phenotypes related to that deficiency.Functionality of the Myc tag has not been confirmed. Immunohistochemistry is not required to see the EGFP fluorescence. 分子注记：The targeting vector used for homologous recombination contained a cre/GFP fusion sequence (cre fused in frame with EGFP at the C-terminus), N-terminal nuclear localization signal and myc tag, and frt-flanked PGK-neo marker. Cre was inserted at the initiation ATG codon in exon 2 of the gene. Chimeric animals were bred with Flper mice to remove the PGK-neo selection marker."
