      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, these mice are bred by homozygote sibling matings. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N12+pN2F1",
      "detailed_desc": "Mx1gfp mice have an inducible GFP/ovalbumin (OVA) fusion gene inserted into the translation start site of the MX dynamin-like GTPase 1 (Mx1) gene. C57BL/6 mice (and many other inbred mice) carry the Mx1s1 allele, a viral susceptibility allele with a deletion of exons 9-11 that results in an MX1 protein that cannot provide resistance to influenza virus. The endogenous Mx1 promoter is silent in healthy mice, but is induced to high levels of transcription by administration of interferon beta (type I), interferon lambda (type III), synthetic double-stranded RNA (such as poly I:C) or by infection with virus. Insertion of the GFP/OVA fusion gene does not functionally alter MX1 activity, and can be used as a reporter for interferon signaling. Mice homozygous for this allele are viable and fertile. The GFP reporter can be used to study cell types, localization, and kinetics of interferon responding cells during virus infection. OVA epitopes can be used to track T cell responses. 分子注记：The targeting construct is designed to insert a GFP reporter-GSGGS-OVA(229-359) fusion protein followed by an ACN cassette into exon 2 (the natural translation start site) of the gene. The ACN cassette includes a neomycin cassette, Cre recombinase and testes specific promoter (tACE) flanked by loxP sites. The tACE promoter allows expression of cre during spermatogenesis resulting in removal of the ACN cassette."
