      "detailed_desc": "Ager (advanced glycosylation end product-specific receptor) encodes a cell surface multiligand receptor that mediates interactions of advanced glycosylation end products (AGE) as well as molecules involved in homeostasis, development, and inflammation. Ager-H2b:Venus knock-in reporter mice express a Venus variant yellow fluorescent protein from the endogenous Ager locus. Venus is detected in Type 1 alveolar (AT1) epithelial cells using antibodies to GFP. AT1 cells cover 95% of the internal surface of the lung and are involved in gas exchange. Mice homozygous for the mutation are viable and fertile with no overt phenotype. These mice may be useful for tracking lung alveolar cell proliferation and differentiation. 分子注记：A cassette encoding H2b:Venus fusion protein followed by poly and a FRT flanked neo cassette were recombined into the start codon of Ager gene by homologous recombination."
