      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony HOM HOM expected to be viable and fertile on normal chow diet. On an atherogenic diet, mice may have a shortened life span. Mating scheme: Heterozygous for Scarb1tm1.1Okoch Heterozygous for Ldlrtm1Her&nbsp; X Heterozygous for Scarb1tm1.1Okoch Heterozygous for Ldlrtm1Her Coat color: Various Generation: pF1N?+F1pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "SR-BI&Delta;CT/LDLR KO mice produce truncated SCARB1 and truncated non-functional LDLR protein. Double homozygous mice are viable and fertile when maintained on a normal chow diet. When fed an atherogenic (Paigen) diet starting at 6 weeks of age, these mice exhibit cardiac pathologies including rapid onset and fatal, occlusive coronary arterial atherosclerosis, myocardial infarction and premature death (median age of death: 9 weeks). When fed a Western-type atherogenic diet the mice exhibit major adverse cardiovascular events, including spontaneous plaque rupture with MI and stroke and premature death (&gt;80% mortality after 26 weeks). Thus, these mice are useful for studying coronary heart disease and stroke. The SR-BI&Delta;CT allele contains a point mutation at amino acid 507 which introduces a premature stop codon within the carboxy terminal in exon 12 of the scavenger receptor class B, member 1 (Scarb1) gene. This mutation produces a truncated protein that is missing 3 C-terminal amino acids (507AKL509). The steady state levels of this truncated protein in the liver are very low relative to the levels of the full-length protein in wildtype mice. Residual levels of receptor protein in the adrenal glands, ovaries, and testes appears sufficient to maintain nearly normal cholesteryl ester (CE) stores. Mice singly homozygous for the SR-BI&Delta;CT allele are viable and fertile and have hypercholesterolemia. Mice singly homozygous for the Ldlrtm1Her mutation have an elevated serum cholesterol level of 200-400 mg/dl and they have very high levels (&gt;2,000 mg/dl) when fed a high fat diet. Normal serum cholesterol in the mouse is 80-100 mg/dl. The SR-BI&Delta;CT/LDLR KO mice (Stock No. 033709) was assembled by breeding Stock No. 032062 to Stock No. 002207. In an attempt to offer alleles on well-characterized or multiple genetic backgrounds, alleles are frequently moved to a genetic background different from that on which an allele was first characterized. It should be noted that the phenotype of these mice could vary from that originally described. We may modify the strain description if necessary as published results become available. 分子注记：Insertion of a neomycin resistance cassette into exon 4. The authors predict that the targeted allele would encode a truncated non-functional protein that will not bind LDL, and that lacks a membrane spanning segment. Immunoblot analysis of liver membranes detected a truncated protein in homozygous mutant animals. The ta"
