      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, hemizygous mice may be bred to wildtype siblings, or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Homozygous viability/fertility has not been tested (August 2019). Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "TRE-COX2 mice express rat Ptgs2, prostaglandin-endoperoxide synthase 2, under the control of a tet-responsive element (tetO; also called tetracycline-responsive element [TRE, TetRE] or tet-operator). When these transgenic mice are bred with other transgenic mice expressing reverse tetracycline-controlled transactivator protein (rtTA) or tetracycline-controlled transactivator protein (tTA), tissue-specific Ptgs2 expression can be regulated with the tetracycline analog doxycycline. No transgene expression is detected in mice stimulated with doxycycline. Mice hemizygous for the TRE-COX2 transgene are viable and fertile. Homozygous viability/fertility has not been tested (August 2019). When crossed to Rosa26-rtTA mice and treated with doxycycline, the resulting double mutant mice develop symptoms of fever (hypodynamia, anorexia, ruffled fur, cessation of exploratory behavior, and social withdrawal). No transgene expression is detected in double mutant mice not treated with doxycycline. When crossed to villin-rtTA2-M2 mice (with rtTA expression in the intestinal epithelium) and treated with doxycycline, Ptgs2 is detected in the intestine and not in the liver of the resulting double mutant mice. 分子注记：The transgenic construct contains a 5.6 kb rat Ptgs2 gene under the control of the tetO, tetracycline-responsive regulatory element and viral VP16 hybrid promoter."
