      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred to wildtype siblings, or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Homozygotes are not viable due to loss of norepinephrine synthesis. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Wild-type; Wild-type x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N17+pN3F2",
      "detailed_desc": "These Dbhcre knock-in mice express Cre recombinase from the endogenous Dbh (dopamine beta hydroxylase) locus, directing Cre recombinase activity in noradrenergic and adrenergic neurons. Insertion of Cre abolishes Dbh gene expression. The targeted Dbh gene encodes an oxidoreductase that catalyzes the oxidative hydroxylation of dopamine to norepinephrine. Mutations in this gene have been associated with Orthostatic Hypotension 1. Mice that are heterozygous for the targeted mutation are viable and fertile. Homozygotes are not viable (embryonic lethal) due to loss of norepinephrine synthesis. 分子注记：A rox-flanked transcriptional stop cassette, cre cDNA, rabbit beta-globin polyadenylation cassette, and attB/attP-flanked neomycin resistance cassette were inserted into the Dbh locus, immediately following the start codon by homologous recombination. A recombinant clone was transiently transfected with pPGKPhiC31obpa to excise the neomycin resistance cassette before cells were injected into blastocysts to produce chimeric mice. Following germline transmission, heterozygotes were crossed with Dre expressing mice to remove the rox-flanked stop cassette."
