      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Adcyap1-2A-CreER knock-in mice express a CreERT2 (CreERT2) fusion protein from the Adcyap1 (adenylate cyclase activating polypeptide 1) promoter/enhancer elements. CreERT2 fusion gene activity is inducible and observed following tamoxifen administration. As such, when Adcyap1-2A-CreER mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequence(s), tamoxifen-inducible Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequence(s) in ADCYAP1-positive neurons in neocortex and pons of the offspring. The donating investigator reports that there is no Cre recombinase activity before tamoxifen treatment. No other tissues were tested for Cre recombinase activity. Endogenous Adcyap1 gene expression is not altered by the knock-in insert. Homozygous mice are viable and fertile. 分子注记：A targeting vector was designed to insert an internal ribosome entry site (IRES) fused to a CreER fusion gene followed by a frt-flanked neo cassette upstream of the stop codon of the adenylate cyclase activating polypeptide 1 (Adcyap1) gene. CreER incorporates cre recombinase fused to a G400V/M543A/L544A triple mutation of the human estrogen receptor ligand binding domain. The neomycin cassette was excised with Flp recombinase."
