      "detailed_desc": "CRISPR/cas9 endonuclease mediated genome editing of the SRY (sex determining region Y)-box 9 (Sox9) gene was used to introduce an IRES-Cre/ERT2-SV40pA cassette into the 3&rsquo; UTR, in these Sox9-CreER mice. These mice have both endogenous gene and Cre recombinase expression directed to Sox9-expressing cells by the endogenous promoter/enhancer elements of the Sox9 gene. The Sox9 gene encodes a transcription factor important in chondrogenesis, and skeletal, endocrine, and epidermal development, as well as sex determination. Restricted to the cytoplasm, cre-ERT2 can only gain access to the nuclear compartment after exposure to tamoxifen. When Sox9-CreER mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequences, tamoxifen-inducible Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the Cre-expressing cells of the offspring. Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile, the donating investigator did not attempt to make a homozygous colony. When bred with Rosa26 reporter strain Ai14 (Stock No. 007914), Sox9-expressing hair follicle stem cells and their progenitor cells can be permanently marked upon tamoxifen injection for postnatal lineage tracing. 分子注记：A cDNA encoding IRES-cre recombinase fused with a mutant form of estrogen receptor hormone-binding domain C (ERT2) was inserted after the site encoding the translational stop codon of the Sox9 gene, using the CRISPR/Cas9 technology."
