      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygotes may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N2+pN1F3",
      "detailed_desc": "CCR2-CreER-GFP mice express a codon-improved icre-ERT2 and EGFP directed from the endogenous chemokine (C-C motif) receptor 2 (Ccr2) promoter. CCR2 encodes a receptor for monocyte chemoattractant protein-1, a chemokine that specifically mediates monocyte chemotaxis, and is expressed on monocytes and macrophages, but not in microglia or tissue resident macrophage at the resting state. These mice express icre-ERT2 and GFP protein in monocytes. Restricted to the cytoplasm, icre-ERT2 can only gain access to the nuclear compartment after exposure to tamoxifen. Homozygotes are viable and fertile. When these mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequence, tamoxifen-inducible cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the cre-expressing cells of the offspring. GFP fluorescence is detectable via fluorescence-activated cell sorting (FACS), immunohistochemistry, and direct fluorescence. Using FACS and single-cell RT-PCR, 95.6% of GFP-positive bone marrow cells (BMCs) are Ccr2-positive, whereas all GFP-negative BMCs are Ccr2-negative. In addition, 98.0% of GFP-positive peripheral blood cells (PBCs) are Ccr2-positive, while all GFP-negative PBCs are Ccr2-negative. 分子注记：Plasmids encoding a guide RNA was designed to insert a improved icre-ER fusion gene (an iCre recombinase fused to a human estrogen receptor ligand binding domain) between exon 3 and the 3' UTR of the chemokine (C-C motif) receptor 2 (Ccr2) gene. An enhanced green fluorescent protein (EGFP) sequence was inserted downstream of the icre-ER, and viral P2A oligopeptides, from porcine teschovirus-1, flank the icre-ER fusion gene to mediate ribosomal skipping."
