      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, mice homozygous for all three alleles are bred by sibling matings, alternatively the colony can be maintained with L121 segregating for use in studies of lower-affinity autoreactive B cells. Mating scheme: Homozygous for Jtm1Dim Homozygous for Igh-Jtm1Dim Homozygous for H2g7 X Homozygous for Jtm1Dim Homozygous for Igh-Jtm1Dim Homozygous for H2g7 Coat color: Black",
      "detailed_desc": "H121 L121 (121) mice carry rearranged VHDHJH and VLJL sequence (respectively) from the anti-GPI mAb 6.121 derived from a mouse model of inflammatory rheumatoid arthritis, K/BxN (Tg(TcraR28,TcrbR28)KRNDimxNODF1). mAb 6.121 is an IgG1 mAb that has a high binding affinity for glucose-6-phosphate isomerase (GPI), a widely expressed blood borne enzyme and the target autoantigen in the K/BXN model. In addition, 121 mice carry the diabetogenic H2g7 haplotype. A high fraction of B cells from 121 mice are reactive to GPI self-antigen, specifically, the bone marrow has an increase in immature B cells and proportionate decrease in mature B cells, as well as increased IgG (anti-GPI) and IgM (anti-GPI). Triple homozygotes have a higher percentage of autoreactive B cells than heterozygotes. H121 L121 (121) mice do not develop arthritis and homozygotes are normal in viability and fertility. 121 mice may be useful in the study of B cell tolerance to a natural self-antigen. 分子注记：A targeting vector containing the mAb 6.121 VkJk sequence and a loxP-flanked neomycin cassette was inserted into the locus to replace the Jk region. Cre mediated recombination subsequently removed the neomycin cassette upon transmission from male chimeric mice. A targeting vector containing the mAb 6.121 VHDHJH sequence and a loxP-flanked neomycin resistance cassette was inserted into the locus to replace the JH region. Cre mediated recombination subsequently removed the neomycin cassette upon transmission from male chimeric mice."
