      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N5+pN2F1",
      "detailed_desc": "Mutations in genes encoding lysosomal proteins cause severe disorders collectively known as lysosomal storage diseases (LSDs). Many LSDs are associated with neurodegeneration, indicating a critical role for the lysosome in neuronal homeostasis. Consistent with this, human genetic studies have implicated impaired lysosomal function in several age-associated neurodegenerative diseases, including Alzheimer's disease (AD), Parkinson's disease (PD), and frontotemporal dementia (FTD). LysoTag (Rosa26; lox-stop-lox-Tmem192-3xHA) mice conditionally express human TMEM192 cDNA (encoding a lysosomal transmembrane protein) fused to a hemagglutinin (3xHA) tag upon Cre recombinase-mediated excision of a loxP-flanked STOP cassette. Expression of the HA tag enables rapid, tissue-specific, anti-HA antibody-driven immunoisolation of intact lysosomes for content profiling. 分子注记：A CAG-loxP-neomycin-Stop-loxP-FRT-TMEM192-3xHA-FRT-pA cassette incorporating full-length human TMEM192 cDNA coding sequences fused to a 3x hemagglutinin tag was introduced to intron 1."
