      "breeding_summary": "While maintaining a live colony, these mice are bred as heterozygotes. The donating investigator has not tested homozygous fertility. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Wild-type; Wild-type x Heterozygote Coat color: Various Generation: ?+pN1F1",
      "detailed_desc": "Slc6a3 encodes the dopamine active transporter (DAT) which is responsible for the re-uptake of dopamine from the synaptic cleft in to the pre-synaptic terminal. Dopaminergic neurons are classified into several sub-types and can differ in their projection targets, electrophysiological properties, behavioral influence, and susceptibility to degeneration. DAT has been implicated in a number of dopamine-related disorders, including attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, bipolar disorder, clinical depression, and alcoholism. DAT-Flp knock-in mice have a P2A-FlpO cassette inserted 3' of the stop codon of the solute carrier family 6 (neurotransmitter transporter, dopamine), member 3 (Slc6a3 or DAT) gene. The self-cleaving P2A sequence allows for expression of the endogenous DAT protein and FlpO recombinase, however, please note that expression of DAT is reduced. Mice homozygous for the mutation are viable, however, the donating investigator has not tested homozygous fertility. When these DAT-Flp mice are bred with mice containing an FRT-flanked sequence, FlpO-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the FRT-flanked sequences in dopaminergic neurons of the offspring. These mice are useful for studying circuit function involving dopaminergic neurons, and may also be combined with cre expressing lines for intersectional studies of sub-populations of dopaminergic neurons. 分子注记：CRISPR/cas9 endonuclease-mediated genome editing is used to insert a P2A-Flpo sequence 3' of the stop codon in the final exon (exon 15) of gene sequence."
