      "breeding_summary": "Hemizygotes are viable and fertile, however, mice begin to die at 4-6 months with 38% of mice dying by 8 months of age. Mating scheme: Noncarrier x Hemizygote Coat color: Albino Generation: ?+pN1F1",
      "detailed_desc": "Tpm1 (tropomyosin 1, alpha) encodes a striated muscle thin filament protein that binds actin filaments and provides structural stability as well as regulation of filament function. TPM1 is involved in the regulation of muscle contraction through Ca2+-mediated activation through the troponin complex. Mutations in Tpm1 are associated with dilated and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy. TM54 mice express a murine Tpm1 harboring a glutamic acid to lysine substitution at residue 54 (E54K) under the cardiomyocyte-specific Myh6 promoter. The E54K mutation is associated with dilated cardiomyopathy 1Y. Mice hemizygous for the mutation are viable and fertile but begin dying of heart failure between 4-6 months with 38% dying by 8 months. TM54 mice develop peripheral edema, increased heart weight, dilation of both ventricles, peripheral edema, and myocyte hypertrophy.A companion strain, TM180, carrying the hypertrophic cardiomyopathy E180G mutation in Tpm1 is available as Stock No. 035611. 分子注记：The cardiac specific mouse alpha-MHC promoter drives the expression of a mouse mutant alpha-tropomyosin striated muscle specific cDNA with a single nucleotide change, GAA>AAA, corresponding to an amino acid substitution of a glutamic acid to lysine at codon 54 (Glu54Lys). Five lines were generated; 67, 71, 76, 95, and 30. This line has a copy number of 22 and is one of the moderate-expressing lines."
