      "breeding_summary": "Hemizygotes are viable and fertile, however, mice begin to die at 4 months with 70% of mice dying by 5 months of age. Mating scheme: Noncarrier x Hemizygote Coat color: Albino Generation: ?+pN4F8",
      "detailed_desc": "Tpm1 (tropomyosin 1, alpha) encodes a striated muscle thin filament protein that binds actin filaments and provides structural stability as well as regulation of filament function. TPM1 is involved in the regulation of muscle contraction through Ca2+-mediated activation through the troponin complex. Mutations in Tpm1 are associated with dilated and hypertrophic cardiomyopathy. TM180 mice express a murine Tpm1 harboring a glutamic acid to glycine substitution at residue 180 (E180G) under the cardiomyocyte-specific Myh6 promoter. The E180G mutation is located in the troponin T binding region and is associated with hypertrophic cardiomyopathy 3. Mice hemizygous for the mutation are viable and fertile but begin dying of heart failure around 4 months of age with 70% dying by 5 months. TM180 mice develop lethargy, increased heart size, increased lung weight, cardiac fibrosis in the left ventricular wall, altered cardiac muscle contractility, increased diastolic pressure, and decreased heart rate.A companion strain, TM54, carrying the dilated cardiomyopathy E54K mutation in Tpm1 are available as Stock No. 035610. 分子注记：This transgene consists of the murine alpha-myosin heavy chain cardiac-specific promoter ligated to the 5' end of the mouse alpha-tropomyosin with a single point mutation (GAG to GGG) corresponding to a glycine substitution for a glutamic acid at codon 180. This region interacts with troponin T. Quantification of the transgene demonstrates that copy number in line 57 is 22 copies."
