      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N5F10",
      "detailed_desc": "These Il17aCre knock-in/knock-out mice possess a codon improved Cre recombinase (icre) and a polyadenylation signal (polyA) into exon 1, as well as a point mutation in exon 2 to disable the internal START codon, of the interleukin 17A (Il17a) gene. This targeted mutation abolishes Il17a expression. Homozygotes are viable, fertile, and normal in size. IL17A is a proinflammatory cytokine produced by T helper cells which recruits monocytes and neutrophils to sites of inflammation. When these Il17aCre mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequence, iCre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the Il17a-expressing cells of the offspring. Breeding these mice to Gt(ROSA)26Sortm1(EYFP)Cos reporter mice allows fluorescent labeling of cells expressing IL17A. These mice may be useful for fate mapping IL17A secretion during T helper cell activation. 分子注记：A codon-improved cre recombinase gene, preceded by a 5-codon linker sequence and followed by an SV40 intron and poly(A) signal sequences, was inserted immediately after the endogenous start codon in exon 1. Point mutations were introduced into exon 2 of the Il17a gene to disable an internal ATG-site. The neomycin resistance gene cassette that was inserted downstrea of the cre gene was excised by FLPe-mediated recombination to generate the the final allele."
