      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together.&nbsp; Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N1+pN1F1",
      "detailed_desc": "ER-BioIDHA (secretome) knock-in mice have Cre-inducible widespread, or tissues-specific, expression of a ER-BioID2HA fusion protein. Specifically, the transgene has a CMV enhancer/chicken beta-actin (CAG) promoter, a floxed cassette containing a green fluorescent protein sequence (EGFP) and a polyadenylation signal, followed by the ER-BioID2HA coding sequence. ER-BioID2HA is composed of an IgK signal peptide, BioID2 coding sequence (containing a mutant biotin ligase (BirA*) sequence), a hemagglutinin (HA) tag, and the endoplasmic reticulum (ER) retention signal KDEL (Lys-Asp-Glu-Leu) tetrapeptide. Proximity-dependent biotin identification (BioID) is based on expression of a \"bait\" protein fused to a promiscuous biotin ligase (BirA*) that generates a history of the bait's proximity-dependent associations over a period by the biotinylation of interacting or neighboring \"prey\" proteins. This strain contains a second generation version, BioID2, which incorporated a smaller ligase that functions optimally at lower temperatures. After breeding to a Cre-expressing line, these secretome mice secrete biotinylated proteins in a tissue-specific fashion when given exogenous biotin in their diet. These biotinylated serum proteins can be rapidly identified using a simple one-step streptavidin purification followed by mass spectroscopy. When bred to VE-Cadherin-Cre mice (Stock No. 006137) to delete the LSL cassette only in endothelial cells, serum from the resulting secretomeENDO mice contains biotinylated von Willebrand factor and secreted forms of endothelial cell surface receptors such as VEGFR-3, VCAM1, PECAM1, and cadherin-5. The serum also contains proteins not commonly associated with the endothelium, such as fibrocystin (Pkhd1l1). When bred to MCK-Cre mice (Stock No. 006475) to delete the LSL cassette only in skeletal muscle cells, serum from the resulting secretomeMUSCLE mice contains biotinylated circulating myostatin when fed biotin supplementation for 5 days. These tagged myostatin levels are reduced when mice are exercised. Of note, ER-BioIDHA itself is not detectable in the serum, suggesting the biotinylation enzyme is not directly secreted, or is secreted at a very low level, into the circulation. Homozygotes are viable and fertile. The donating investigator reports that EGFP expression is visible via direct fluorescence using GoBe-LAND flashlight from NIGHTSEA prior to Cre-excision. 分子注记：The transgenic construct contains a CMV enhancer/chicken beta-actin "
