      "detailed_desc": "Orai1fl/fl mice have loxP sites flanking exon 2 of the ORAI calcium release-activated calcium modulator 1 (Orai1) gene. Orai1 encodes a major component of the calcium release-activated calcium (CRAC) channel. CRAC channels consist of two major components, the plasma membranelocalized pore subunit, ORAI1, and an ER-resident Ca2+ sensor, STIM1. STIM1 senses depletion of the ER Ca2+ stores and interacts with ORAI1 to open the pore. High and sustained signaling mediated by the CRAC channels is essential for the induction of transcriptional programs via the NFAT pathway. Severe combined immune deficiency (SCID) caused by mutations in ORAI1 and STIM1 and the widespread use of inhibitors of this pathway, cyclosporine A and FK506 in clinics, underscore the importance of therapeutic targeting of the Ca2+-NFAT pathway. Global knockouts of Orai1 are embryonically lethal in the C57BL6/J genetic background. These conditionally targeted homozygous mice (Orai1fl/fl) are viable and fertile. When these mutant mice are bred to mice that express Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have exon 2 deleted in Cre-expressing tissues. These mice are useful for studies requiring tissue specific deletion of Orai1. 分子注记：Exon 2 was flanked by loxP sites and a FRT-flanked neomycin resistance gene cassette was inserted. Flp-mediated recombination removed the selection cassette."
