      "breeding_summary": "While maintaining a live colony, these mice are bred as homozygous for both alleles. These mice are immunodeficient and need to be maintained in a high barrier environment with sterile food, water and cage. Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Rag2 (recombination activating gene 2) encodes a protein involved in the initiation of V(D)J recombination during B and T cell development. Rag1 and Rag2 form the two core components of the RAG complex; a recombinase responsible for double-stranded DNA breaks at conserved recombination signal sequences. Thy1.1 RAG-/- Balb/c mice contain a neomycin cassette designed to replace a 0.85kb segment of the Rag2 open reading frame, abolishing RAG2 function and the Thy1a (Thy1.1) allelic variant on a BALB background. Mice homozygous for both alleles are viable, fertile, and normal in size, but should be considered immunodeficient. Rag2 KO mice lack mature T and B cells. These mice may be useful for studying roles of RAG2 in B and T cell development, T and B cell receptor recombination, hematopoiesis, hematology, immunology, and inflammation research. The addition of the Thy1a allele to the Rag2 knockout (KO) provides a tracking option for adoptive transfer studies and allows for more accurate tracking of transferred cells (either as recipients or donors). 分子注记：A neomycin resistance cassette replaced a 0.85kb segment of the open reading frame, eliminating the encoding of 286 of the 527 amino acids of the protein. The allele Thy1a determines an antigenic specificity, Thy-1.1, found in the AKR and RF strains."
