      "breeding_summary": "Hemizygous mice are viable and fertile. Homozygote viability/fertility has not been assessed. The donating investigator indicates that Cre inactivation or Cre activity may occur in the male germline. LratCre females, but not males, must be used for breeding; breeding through the male may permanently alter cre activity. Mating scheme: Hemizygote x Noncarrier Generation: N7+pN2",
      "detailed_desc": "LratCre BAC transgenic mice express cre recombinase under the direction of the mouse Lrat (lecithin-retinol acyltransferase [phosphatidylcholine-retinol-O-acyltransferase]) promoter elements. Lrat encodes a microsomal enzyme involved in the formation of retinyl ester-containing lipid droplets, one of the features of hepatic stellate cells (HSC). Hepatic stellate cells are a pericyte-like cell population that are a major source of hepatic myofibroblasts in models of toxic, cholestatic and fatty liver disease. Western blot analysis of LratCre mice detects high cre expression in hepatic stellate cells, but almost undetectable expression in hepatocytes, Kupffer cells, endothelial cells, and colangiocytes. When crossed with a strain containing loxP sites flanking the sequence of interest, the offspring are useful for generating cre-mediated targeted gene deletions in hepatic stellate cells, with only minimal deletion in other liver cell populations. LratCre transgenic mice can delete loxP-flanked genes in other organs. Hemizygous mice are viable and fertile. Homozygote viability/fertility has not been assessed. LratCre females, but not males, must be used for breeding; breeding through the male may permanently alter cre activity.&nbsp; Both males and females can be used in experiments. This strain may be useful for in vivo lineage tracing and functional analysis of hepatic stellate cells in liver fibrosis. 分子注记：A construct containing a cassette encoding cre recombinase as well as a neo selection cassette was inserted by recombineering methods into a BAC at the ATG codon of the Lrat locus. The neo was removed by arabinose-induced flippase. Purified BAC DNA was injected into pronuclei of fertilized oocytes. Six founders were positive for the transgene and the line with the strongest cre activity in liver and hemotopoietic stem cells was used for further studies."
