      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, hemizygous mice may be bred to wildtype siblings or to FVB/NJ inbred mice. The Donating Investigator has not attempted to make this strain homozygous. Mating scheme: Hemizygote x Noncarrier; Noncarrier x Hemizygote Coat color: Albino Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "BAC-CAG transgenic mice express a neuropathogenic, full-length human mutant Huntingtin gene modified to harbor 120 CAG repeats followed by one CAA, 8 CAGs and another CAA-CAG encoding a total of 131 glutamine repeats under the control of endogenous human HTT regulatory machinery. Mice hemizygous for the BAC-CAG transgene are viable and fertile. Like other full length human HTT mouse models, BAC-CAG hemizygotes exhibit multiple phenotypes including progressive rotarod deficits (6 months), hypolocomotion (12 months), sleep disturbance (12 months), and striatal synapse loss (12 months). In addition, the BAC-CAG model, which lacks the numerous CAA interruptions in the DNA sequences encoding the mHTT polyQ stretch found in BACHD mice (FVB/N-Tg(HTT*97Q)IXwy/J, Stock No. 008197), develops additional key Huntington's disease (HD) phenotypes such as minimal body weight gain, decrease in grip strength, striatal and cortical somatical CAG repeat instabilities correlated with behavioral impairment (locomotor activity/sleep), striatal astrocytosis and microgliosis, striatal and deeper cortical layers-selective mHTT aggregation and nuclear inclusions, and robust age-dependent and striatum-selective transcriptional dysregulation in 12-month-old mice. These mice may be useful in the testing of candidate therapeutics and in understanding the pathogenesis of Huntington's disease-like phenotypes in vivo. 分子注记：The 240 kb human bacterial artificial chromosome (BAC) RP11-866L6, containing the entire 170 kb human Huntingtin (HTT) genomic locus and approximately 20 kb of 5' and 50 kb of 3' flanking sequences, was modified by replacing the human mutant mHTT exon 1 sequence (containing about 120 CAG repeats followed by one CAA, 8 CAGs and another CAA-CAG encoding a total of about 131 glutamine repeats). Founder line BAC-CAG contains 2 tandem copies of the transgene. mHTT repeat sizing and sequencing confirmed an uninterrupted CAG repeat size of about 120, with total polyQ repeat sequence of 131."
