      "breeding_summary": "Ctla4+/- Pdcd1-/- mice develop organ-specific autoimmunity leading to premature death in approximately half of mice (median survival ~100 days). The strain can be propagated through intercrosses of Ctla4+/- Pdcd1-/- mice (heterozygous for the Ctla4 knock-out allele and homozygous for the Pdcd1 knock-out allele), or by crossing Ctla4+/‐ Pdcd1‐/‐ males with female Ctla4+/+ Pdcd1‐/‐ mice (wildtype for Ctla4 and homozygous for the Pdcd1 knock-out allele) to avoid any potential autoimmunity or fetal-maternal tolerance issues. The frequency of mortality in Ctla4+/- Pdcd1-/- mice is reported to be partially sex-dependent, with female mice dying at higher frequency than males. Mice homozygous for both the Ctla4 and Pdcd1 knock-out alleles are embryonic/perinatal lethal, and 100% of mice homozygous for the Ctla4 knock-out alone succumb to a massive lymphoproliferative disease at ~1 month. Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICI) targeting CTLA4 (cytotoxic T-lymphocyte-associated protein 4) or PDCD1 (programmed cell death 1; also called PD-1/PD-L1) have shown remarkable efficacy across multiple tumor types but are associated with immune-related adverse events, including myocarditis. ICI-associated myocarditis is characterized by myocardial T-cell and macrophage infiltration and significant ECG disturbances. Mice that are heterozygous for a Ctla4 knock-out allele and homozygous for a Pdcd1 knock-out allele (Ctla4+/- Pdcd1-/-) provide a robust preclinical mouse model of ICI-associated myocarditis. Ctla4+/- Pdcd1-/- mice develop organ-specific autoimmunity leading to premature death in approximately half of mice (median survival ~100 days). Premature death results from myocardial infiltration by T cells and macrophages and severe ECG abnormalities, closely recapitulating the clinical and pathologic hallmarks of ICI-associated myocarditis observed in patients. The frequency of mortality is reported to be partially sex-dependent, with female mice dying at higher frequency than males, consistent with the characteristics of ICI-associated myocarditis in patients. Mice that succumb to premature death may exhibit some clinical signs prior to death (e.g., reduced body weight gain, reduced movement, and dyspnea as early as 1 month of age), but most mice appear normal. Approximately 25% of mice survive beyond 1 year. Mice homozygous for both the Ctla4 and Pdcd1 knock-out alleles are embryonic/perinatal lethal, and 100% of mice homozygous for the Ctla4 knock-out alone succumb to a massive lymphoproliferative disease at ~1 month. 分子注记：The insertion of neomycin selection cassette under the control of a PGK promoter disrupted exon 3. A floxed neo cassette was inserted upstream of exon 2 and an additional loxP site was inserted downstream of exon 3. Transient cre expression in ES cells removed exons 2 and 3 along with the neo cassette."
