      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN1F2",
      "detailed_desc": "Pigrfl/fl mice possess loxP sites flanking exons 5-10 of the polymeric immunoglobulin receptor (Pigr) gene. PIGR encodes a transmembrane protein receptor expressed in the mouse hepatobiliary tract that facilitates immunoglobulin (Ig)A and IgM transport from serum to the gut epithelial surface, specifically to the small intestinal lumen. Mice that are homozygous for this floxed allele are viable and fertile. When bred to mice that express tissue-specific Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have exons 5-10 deleted in the Cre-expressing tissues. When bred to Alb-cre mice (see Stock No. 003574), resulting HB-pIgR KO mice exhibit no differences in body weight, fertility, litter size, or gut epithelial barrier. Fecal bacterial populations in HB-pIgR KO mice are distinct from wildtype mice, with a shift towards communities more commonly encountered in the human gut, including members of the Prevotella genera. These mice may be useful for studying innate immunity and for modeling microbial dynamics in the human gut microbial equilibrium. 分子注记：The targeting vector is designed to insert a loxP site upstream of exon 5 and an FRT-flanked neomycin selection cassette, followed by a second loxP site, downstream of exon 10. Flp-mediated recombination removed the FRT-flanked neo cassette."
