      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "The SEP-GluA1 KI mice have a pH-sensitive super ecliptic pHluorin (SEP) variant of green fluorescent protein (GFP) fused to the extracellular N-terminus of the glutamate receptor, ionotropic, AMPA1 (alpha 1) (Gria1) gene by insertion into exon 1, resulting in the expression of a SEP-GluA1 fusion protein. Gria1 encodes an AMPA receptor subunit that has been found to regulate synaptic plasticity. SEP is a pH-sensitive variant of GFP that enables visualization of only the functional complement of AMPARs on the cell surface since SEP fluoresces at neutral pH, while the fluorescence of receptors localized in acidic, internal compartments such as endosomes and Golgi is quenched. Homozygous SEP-GluA1 KI mice exhibit a slight decrease in GluA1 mRNA and protein expression in the postsynaptic density (56.6% of WT mice) and in total membrane protein levels (44.4% of WT). They also display slight increases in the expression levels of GluA2 and GluA3 subunits. All GluA1 receptors express SEP in SEP-GluA1 KI mice. Synapses with fluorescently labeled AMPARs function identically to wildtype synapses, with no discernible differences in the amplitude, frequency, or kinetics of miniature excitatory postsynaptic currents (EPSCs) or alteration of the EPSCs. Also, SEP-tagged GluA1 receptors are properly trafficked to the postsynaptic site and colocalized normally with other postsynaptic proteins. Mice that are homozygous for this allele are viable and fertile. SEP fluorescence is detectable by direct fluorescence in vivo or in vitro, and also by immunohistochemistry by using an anti-GFP antibody. 分子注记：The targeting vector is designed to fuse a pH-sensitive super ecliptic pHluorin (SEP) variant of green fluorescent protein (GFP) sequence to the extracellular N-terminus by insertion into exon 1. A loxP-flanked neomycin resistance (neo) cassette was inserted downstream of exon 1. Cre-mediated recombination removed the loxP-flanked neo cassette."
