      "breeding_summary": "Il2rg is X linked. Animals homozygous for the remaining alleles and hemizygous (males)/homozygous (females) for the Il2rg mutation are viable and fertile. SPF (specific pathogen-free) conditions are recommended. Please see our NSG housing and breeding information for additional details. Mating scheme: Homozygous for Flt3em2Mvw, Homozygous for Prkdcscid, Homozygous for Il2rgtm1Wjl, Homozygous for Tg(FLT3LG)7Sz, Homozygous for Tg(IL15)1Sz x&nbsp;Homozygous for&nbsp;Flt3em2Mvw, Homozygous for&nbsp;Prkdcscid, Hemizygous for&nbsp;Il2rgtm1Wjl, Homozygous for Tg(FLT3LG)7Sz, Homozygous for Tg(IL15)1Sz Coat color: Albino Generation: F5p",
      "detailed_desc": "NSG-Tg(Hu-IL15); NSG Flt3KO hFLT3LG Tg mice combine the features of the highly immunodeficient NOD scid gamma (NSG&trade;) mouse (Stock No. 005557) with a transgene expressing human FLT3LG (fms related receptor tyrosine kinase 3 ligand), a knock-out of its receptor Flt3 (Flt3 interacting zinc finger protein 1), and a human IL15 transgene that enhances the development of human NK cells in immunodeficient mice engrafted with human stem cells. This model enables the engraftment of diverse hematopoietic lineages, useful for immuno-oncology, immunology, and infectious disease studies. (See representative engraftment data) SPF (specific pathogen-free) conditions are recommended. Please see our NSG housing and breeding information for additional details. View our Resources for the NSG&trade; mouse model, including: NSG&trade; Mouse Model PortfolioHousing and Breeding Considerations for NSG&trade; MiceFrequently Asked NSG&trade; QuestionsBreakthrough Research Using NSG&trade;Immunodeficient Mouse and Xenograft Host ComparisonsFlow Cytometry Characterization Data for Immunodeficient JAX Strains 分子注记：CRISPR/Cas9 genome editing is used to delete part of exon 6, all of exon 7 and most of exon 8. A T-to-A transversion point mutation at a position corresponding to codon 4046 (codon 4095 in transcript ENSMUST00000023352.8) created a premature stop codon (p.Y4046*). A neomycin resistance cassette replaced part of exon 3 and all of exons 4 - 8 of the gene, resulting in the loss of most of the extracellular domain and all of the transmembrane and cytoplasmic domains of the protein. The transgenic construct consists of a 200 kbp human BAC RP11-620F30 containing the complete human IL15 (interleukin 15) gene. Mice express a physiological level of human IL15 (7.1 +/- 0.3 pg/ml). The transgene was generated from a 13.8 kb BamHI restriction fragment from BAC RP11-360G9 containing the human FLT3LG. The fragment was cloned into pBluescript to eliminate other genes in the BAC."
