      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred to wildtype littermates or C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile, the donating investigator has not developed homozygous mice but expects them to be viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Prl8a2iCre knock-in/knock-out mice express a codon improved Cre recombinase (iCre) under direction of the endogenous prolactin family 8, subfamily a, member 2 (Prl8a2) promoter, and it is expected to abolish endogenous Prl8a2 expression. Also known as decidual Prl-related protein [dPRP], PRL8A2 is a member of the prolactin superfamily which are key regulators of decidual cell signaling. Decidualization of uterine stromal cells, from endometrial stromal fibroblast cells into decidual secretory cells, is an imperative step of embryo implantation and pregnancy establishment. It is vital for survival and plays a role in trophoblast invasion, as well as protection against oxidative stress and maternal immunological rejection. In these Prl8a2iCre mice, iCre is expressed in uterine decidua following embryo attachment from gestational day 5.5 in the primary decidual zone into gestational day 9.5 in the anti-mesometrial region. Cre activity is not dependent on the presence of an embryo and can be induced following artificial decidualization. There is no observed cre activity in the ovary, oviduct, pituitary, or skeletal muscle. When bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequences, cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the cre-expressing cells of the offspring. Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile, the donating investigator has not developed homozygous mice but expects them to be viable and fertile. 分子注记：Using CRISPR/Cas9 endonuclease-mediated genome editing, a donor plasmid designed to insert a codon improved cre recombinase (iCre) and a polyadenylation sequence immediately downstream of the start codon of the prolactin family 8, subfamily a, member 2 (Prl8a2) gene, a single guide RNA (ACTAGCAGTCTTATCCAACCNGG), and the cas9 nuclease with a puromycin resistance sequence were transfected into G4 embryonic stem (ES) cells."
