      "breeding_summary": "This strain is maintained by breeding mice that are hemizygous for Tg(ALB)9463J, homozygous for Tg(FCGRT)32Dcr, heterozygous for Albem12Mvw, and homozygous Fcgrttm1Dcr with mice that are non-carrier for Tg(ALB)9463J, homozygous for Tg(FCGRT)32Dcr, homozygous for Albem12Mvw, and homozygous Fcgrttm1Dcr. Experience at The Jackson Laboratory indicates mating homozygous x homozygous for the Albem12Mvw allele tends to be non-productive. Mating scheme: Hemizygous for Tg(ALB)9463J, Homozygous for Tg(FCGRT)32Dcr, Heterozygous for Alb&lt;em12Mvw&gt;, Homozygous for Fcgrt&lt;tm1Dcr&gt; x&nbsp;Noncarrier for Tg(ALB)9463J, Homozygous for Tg(FCGRT)32Dcr, Homozygous for Alb&lt;em12Mvw&gt;, Homozygous for Fcgrt&lt;tm1Dcr&gt; and reciprocal. Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN1F2",
      "detailed_desc": "Tg32 hAlb-BAC mice harbor a human Fc gamma receptor and transporter (FCGRT) transgene, under control of its own native promoter, as well as a human albumin (ALB) transgene. These mice also harbor Alb knock-out (KO) and Fcgrt KO alleles, resulting in ablation of endogenous Alb and Fcgrt expression. Mice that are homozygous for all alleles are viable with no overt phenotype. It is recommended that mice hemizygous for Tg(ALB)9463J, homozygous for Tg(FCGRT)32Dcr, heterozygous for Albem12Mvw, and homozygous Fcgrttm1Dcr are mated with mice that are non-carrier for Tg(ALB)9463J, homozygous for Tg(FCGRT)32Dcr, homozygous for Albem12Mvw, and homozygous Fcgrttm1Dcr. Experience at The Jackson Laboratory indicates mating homozygous x homozygous for the Albem12Mvw allele tends to be non-productive. Initial validation data indicates that Tg32 hAlb-BAC mice express physiological levels of human serum albumin (HSA) at 25 to 40mg/ml. This Tg32 hAlb-BAC mouse model is a preclinical tool that generates translational Pharmacokinetic (PK) data for albumin-based drugs and provides Pharmacodynamic (PD) data for FcRn inhibitors. Need assistance evaluating antibodies in FcRn mice? Human preclinical pharmacokinetic (PK) analysis is available. See our FcRn full service platform. 分子注记：Exon 4 was targeted by introduction of TALEN mRNA into fertilized B6.Cg-Fcgrttm1Dcr Tg(FCGRT)32Dcr/DcrJ oocytes and the resulting founder screened and found to have a 2 base pair deletion beginning at Chromosome 5 base 90,464,113 (GRCm38.p2) which is predicted to result in a frame shift then a premature stop codon 5 amino acids downstream of the encoded frame shift. By ELISA, heterozgyotes have a decrease in serum albumin of approximately 30 percent and homozygotes have no detectable serum albumin. Sequence from exon 1 and part of exon2 was replaced with a PGK-neo cassette. Quantitative PCR of liver cDNA indicated the absence of mRNA. Western blot analysis of neonatal intestinal extracts failed to reveal protein product. A 34Kb fragment of a BAC containing the entire human FCGRT , Fc fragment of IgG, receptor, transporter, alpha, gene (approximately 11kb) and approximately 10kb of flanking sequence was sublconed into a SuperCos vector. The resulting cosmid was microinjected into fertilized C57BL/6J mouse eggs. Founder line 32 was established. Transgene insertion occurred on Chr 2. An ~120 kb BAC construct was containing the entire human albumin (ALB) gene as well as ~45.9 kb upstream sequences (includin"
