      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred together, to wildtype (noncarrier) mice from the colony or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). The donating investigator reports that homozygous males are sterile. The colony maintained by the The Jackson Laboratory has reported transient hairloss in heterozygotes and homozygotes. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "AAV (adeno-associated virus) vectors are frequently used in virus-based gene therapies. The AAV receptor (AAVR or AU04032) is required for transduction by most serotypes of AAV. Expression of AAVR is required for transduction of most AAV vectors for in vivo transgenesis. Aavr- mice were created using TALEN genome editing to cause a 1 bp deletion causing a frameshift in exon 2 of the AU040320 locus resulting in a null allele. AU040320 has been associated with dyslexia, although no clear phenotypes are seen in mice, and overall mice homozygous for the AU040320 mutation appear to be healthy, although there is some transient hairloss (alopecia). Previously it has been reported that male mice homozygous for a different AU040320 null mutation were sterile due to disruption of acrosome biogenesis on the C57BL/6J background (PMC6039479). This mutation also showed sterility in homozygous males, requiring maintenance of HET males for breeding. Females HOM are fertile. Homozygotes are resistant to AAV transduction. This strain may be useful in testing virus based gene therapies. When combined with the SELECTIV mouse model (C57BL/6J-Igs2tm1(CAG-AU040320/mCherry,-cas9*)Janc/J; Stock No. 037553), which allows cre-inducible overexpression of AAVR, SELECTIV-KO mice prevent transduction of all non-target cell types, thus improving AAV specificity. 分子注记：The gene was targeted via TALEN technology using the primer pairs 5'-TGGGAGTCAAGCCAAGTC-3' and5'-GCCAGGATATTGTTGGCAGA-3'. This mutation comprises a single-nucleotide (T) deletion at position 264 of the 4379-nucleotide GenBank cDNA sequence BC028869.1, resulting in a reading-frame shift."
