      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, double homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygous Homozygous&nbsp;x&nbsp;Homozygous Homozygous Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN1F1",
      "detailed_desc": "The targeted Rps15 gene encodes ribosomal protein S15, a cytoplasmic ribosomal protein that is a component of the 40S subunit and has been found to be activated in various tumors. This mutation is analogous to the human Rps15-S138F mutation associated with malignant transformation of B cells in chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL). CLL is the most common B cell leukemia in adults, involving the peripheral blood and lymphoid organs such as lymph nodes and bone marrow. Rps15-S138F floxed conditional knock-in mice carry an allele with a knock-in sequence of loxP sites flanking copies of exons 3-4 and a STOP codon. cDNA encoding exons 3 and 4, containing a serine to phenylalanine mutation (S138F), were inserted downstream of the second loxP site. This strain also contains a Cd19cre knock-in/knock-out allele present in Stock No. 006785 mice, resulting in removal of STOP codon and subsequent expression of Rps15-S138F specifically in B cells. Heterozygous expression of the S138F mutation disrupts B cell function and induced CLL-like disease in mice at 20 months of age with ~37% penetrance due to upregulation of Myc targets, B cell receptor signaling, and Zap70 expression, all markers of aggressive CLL-like disease. Double homozygous Cd19cre/Rps15-S138F floxed knock-in mice are viable and fertile. 分子注记：The vector contains, from 5' to 3' a loxP site, cDNA encoding exons 3-4 of Rps15, a STOP codon containing 3xSV40 polyA, an FRT-flanked neomycin resistance (neo) cassette, and a second loxP site inserted downstream of endogenous exon 2, replacing endogenous exons 3-4. The cDNA encoding exons 3-4 contains a serine to phenylalanine mutation (S138F) is inserted downstream of the second loxP site. The S138F mutation is analogous to the human Rps15-S138F mutation associated with malignant transformation of B cells in chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL). Flp-mediated recombination removed the neo cassette. In-frame insertion of a cre recombinase gene into the first coding exon followed by an fFRT site flanked neomycin resistance gene cassette. A frameshift mutation was also introduced into exon 5. This allele expresses cre recombinase specifically in B lineage cells throughout development. The FLP recombinase removed the neo cassette."
