      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN1F4",
      "detailed_desc": "&Delta;1+2+3 mice carry CRISPR/cas9 generated deletions of the three NFIL3 binding sites in the -165 kb zinc finger E-box binding homeobox 2 (Zeb2) enhancer in the Rr253 regulator region. ZEB2 is a transcription factor that is repressed during pre-conventional type 1 dendritic cell (cDC1) differentiation yet is required for plasmacytoid dendritic cell (pDC) development. The -165 kb Zeb2 enhancer has three binding sites for NFIL3, which has been shown to repress Zeb2 expression. In this mouse line, all three binding sites have been altered to eliminate NFIL3 binding. This triple mutant line removes Zeb2 expression in myeloid, but not lymphoid progenitors, causing an increase in cDC1 development and the complete loss of pre-cDC2 specification and mature cDC2 development in vivo. These mice have pDCs and B cells, but have decreased monocytes. Homozygous mice are viable and fertile. In contrast, Zeb2delta-165 mice (Stock No. 037707) lack the entire -165 kb Zeb2 enhancer and have no pDCs or monocytes. As such, they have increased susceptibility to viral infection induced death. 分子注记：Using zygotes that already carry the Rr253em4Kmm NFIL3Ã¢Â€Â“C/EBP binding site 1&2-deletion allele, binding site 3 in the Zeb2 enhancer, located ~165 kb upstream, were targeted with an sgRNA (targeting CCACCAGCCGGTGACACACA) and an ssODN template (GCTGAAGTTCACCTCCCCATGGGGGAATGAATCATCAAAATAACCGGTGGAAAACAAGCTAGATCTGACTTGAGCAGTGTGTGTCACCGGCTGGTGGAATTTTTAGAAAGGCAGCAGTTTGGGCTCATCACTGCGGTT) using CRISPR/Cas9 technology, resulting in an allele lacking binding sites 1, 2 and 3."
