      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Wild-type; Wild-type x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN3",
      "detailed_desc": "Interleukin 1 beta (IL1&beta;) is a potent pro-inflammatory cytokine expressed in myeloid-derived cells in response to microbial invasion and tissue injury. This cytokine plays a role in regulating the inflammatory response, as well as cell proliferation, differentiation, and apoptosis. IL-1&beta; has also been implicated in inflammatory pain hypersensitivity by induction of cyclooxygenase-2 (PTGS2/COX2) in the central nervous system (CNS). Mice that are homozygous for this IL-1&beta;fl allele are viable and fertile. When bred to mice that express tissue-specific Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have exon 4 deleted in the cre-expressing tissues. These IL-&beta;fl mice may be useful for studying the role of Ilb1 in inflammatory response pathways and autoimmune diseases. 分子注记：CRISPR/cas9 mediated recombination introduced loxP sites 157 bp upstream and 103 bp downstream of exon 4."
