      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, these mice are bred by FVB/N or wild-type female to K14E7 hemizygous male. Although homozygous mice are viable and fertile, homozygous females have trouble nursing. Mating scheme: Hemizygote x Noncarrier; Noncarrier x Hemizygote Coat color: Albino Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Human papillomavirus type 16 (HPV16) is a high-risk small DNA tumor virus that causes papillomas in skin, genitalia, and the upper respiratory tract. HPV16 is associated with cervical cancer.&nbsp; Cancer cells found in HPV-infected individuals often have the HPV genome integrated into the cellular genome. The integration includes the early region of the HPV genome containing the E6 and E7 genes. In cell cultures E6 can immortalize primary human mammary epithelial cells and E7 can transform primary human keratinocytes. E6 has been found to associate with TRP53 and lead to TRP53 degradation through the ubiquitin proteasome pathway. E7 has been found to associate with RB (retinoblastoma) and interfere with RB binding and inactivation of the E2F transcription factor.K14E7 transgenic (low copy founder 2304) mice carry a human keratin 14 (KRT14) promoter directing expression of E7 gene from human papillomavirus type 16 (HPV16). The KRT14 promoter directs expression to the basal layer of the epithelia. Mice homozygous for the transgene are viable and fertile, however homozygous females have trouble nursing. Stunted growth is seen in some homozygous mice.&nbsp; Hemizygous K14E7 mice develop epidermal hyperplasia (skin, mouth palate, esophagus, forestomach, exocervix), and hyperkeratosis. Mice also exhibit wrinkled skin (neonates), cataracts and scruffy fur. Skin tumors in the torso and limbs develop in 3 out of 30 mice at around 10.6 months of age. &nbsp;Most tumors found in K14E7 mice are benign.Of note, the K14E6 transgenic strain (expressing HPV16 E6) is distributed as FVB/N-Tg(KRT14-HPV16E6)5737Plam/J (Stock No. 037878). 分子注记：This transgene contains a HPV16 fragment (nt79-883) encompassing both the E6 and E7 genes along with promoter, 3'UTR and polyA sequences from human KRT14. Only E7 is expressed due to the presence of a translation termination linker in the N terminal region of the E6 gene. Transgene expression is targeted toward epithelial tissues. Mice derived from founder 2304 had 2 copies of the transgene. Mice derived from founder 2332 had 7-8 copies of the transgene. this is a representative record for lines 2304 and 2332 which have identical phenotypes."
