      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygous mice and homozygous males are viable and fertile, however, homozygous females appear not to breed. Coat color: Black Generation: N7+pN2F1",
      "detailed_desc": "Rosa26TurboID KI knock-in mice use a CAG promoter to direct conditional Cre recombinase-mediated expression of a V5-tagged biotin ligase sequence (TurboID) with a nuclear export signal (NES). TurboID is an engineered biotin ligase that uses ATP to convert biotin into biotin&ndash;AMP, a reactive intermediate that covalently labels proximal proteins (Cho KF, et al Nat Protoc 15, 3971-3999 (2020) PMID 33139955). Homozygous Rosa26TurboID knock-in mice are viable and males are fertile, homozygous females do not appear to breed. Prior to exposure to Cre recombinase TurboID is not expressed. In the presence of cre, the STOP cassette is excised allowing TurboID expression in cre-expressing tissues. These mice provide a tool for in vivo biotinylation of proteins allowing characterization of specific proteomes in multiple tissues. When TurboID mice are combined with mice expressing a tamoxifen-inducible Cre recombinase with expression in Camk2a-expressing excitatory neurons (Tg(Camk2a-cre/ERT2)1Aibs; Stock No. 012362), resulting progeny treated with tamoxifen and biotin supplementation develop robust biotinylation of proteins with the highest expression in the cortex, hippocampus, and striatum/thalamus regions. Mice exhibit no adverse reactions to biotin supplementation. Biotinylation is observed within cell bodies and axonal projections in all brain regions sampled and can be used for proteonomic analysis. When TurboID mice are combined with mice expressing a tamoxifen-inducible Cre recombinase with expression in mature astrocytes (Tg(Aldh1l1-cre/ERT2)1Khakh; Stock No. 031008), resulting progeny treated with tamoxifen and biotin supplementation have biotinylation in Gfap- and Ndrg2-positive astrocytes primarily in the hippocampus with no evidence of gliosis. 分子注记：The targeting construct inserted into the locus a CAG promoter, floxed stop cassette, V5-tagged biotin ligase (TurboID), and nuclear export signal."
