      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live congenic colony, mice that are hemizygous for the co-injected transgenes may be bred together, to wildtype (non-carrier) mice from the colony, or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). The donating investigator reports that homozygotes are born at lower than Mendelian rates (2 homozygotes out of 41 offspring produced from hemizygous breeders), and they do not produce viable offspring. Mating scheme: Hemizygote x Noncarrier; Noncarrier x Hemizygote Coat color: Black Generation: N15+pN1F2",
      "detailed_desc": "APPPS1 mice contain the co-injected APPSwe and PSEN1*L166P transgenes under direction of a neuron-specific Thy1 promoter element. APPPS1 mice develop cerebral beta-amyloidosis with very early onset starting at 4-6 weeks. Amyloid-associated pathologies include dystrophic synaptic boutons, hyperphosphorylated tau-positive neuritic structures and robust gliosis, with neocortical microglia number increasing threefold from 1 to 8 months of age. Global neocortical neuron loss is not apparent (at least up to 8 months of age), but local neuron loss in the dentate gyrus is observed. Early and rapid onset of amyloid deposition approaches a plateau, mimicking the phenotype seen in Alzheimer's disease patients before development of neurodegeneration and clinical symptoms. Mice also show fluid core biomarker changes as seen in Alzheimer's disease. Mice breed well as hemizygotes and have no obvious phenotype except for occasional epileptic seizures. The donating investigator reports that homozygotes are born at lower than Mendelian rates (2 homozygotes out of 41 offspring produced from hemizygous breeders), and they do not produce viable offspring. APPPS1 mice die prematurely with an approximate life span of 20-22 months. These mice may be useful for studying cerebral amyloid deposition and related fluid biomarker changes. 分子注记：The Thy1-APPKM670/671NL was constructed with the mutant human APPKM670/671NL cDNA (Swedish or KM670/671NL mutation of amyloid precursor protein (APP)) placed downstream of the murine Thy1.2 promoter region. Additionally, the Thy1-PS1L166P transgene was constructed with a mutant human PS1L166P cDNA (leucine to proline mutation at position 166 of human presenilin 1 (Alzheimer disease 3, PSEN1 or PS1)) placed downstream of the murine Thy1.2 promoter sequences. These constructs were coinjected to produce founder mice. In addition to line 21, lines 5 and 8 were also established."
