      "breeding_summary": "As of January 2023, Ai203 heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. However in March 2026, the donating laboratory states that TIGRE knock-in alleles with long stretch of repetitive sequence and multiple transcription units could potentially lead to instability and unequal cross-over during meiosis. As such, the donating laboratory strongly recommends maintaining this strain as heterozygous. When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred together, to wildtype mice from the colony or to C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Mating scheme: Heterozygote x +/+ sibling Generation: N7+pN1F3",
      "detailed_desc": "Ai203 mice harbor the TITL-sChroME-Kv2.1-GC7s-WPRE-ICL-nls-mRuby3-IRES2-tTA2-WPRE conditional allele, designed with a tetO promoter, loxP-STOP-loxP cassette and sChroME*/GCaMP7s sequence, and then a CAG promoter, Lox2272-STOP-Lox2272 cassette, mRuby3, and IRES-tTA2-WPRE sequence. sChroME is a soma-targeted (ST) ultrafast and highly potent opsin with 3-5&times; larger photocurrents than opsins commonly used for multiphoton optogenetics. sChroME*/GCaMP7s is the result of a sChroME* coupled to the fluorescent reporter GCaMP7s (an ultrasensitive EGFP fluorescent calcium detector of neuronal activity with slow decay and response kinetics). Prior to recombinase exposure, this allele is designed to have the two STOP cassettes preventing expression of the downstream genes (sChroME*/GCaMP7s, mRuby3, and tTA2). As of January 2023, Ai203 heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. However in March 2026, the donating laboratory states that TIGRE knock-in alleles with long stretch of repetitive sequence and multiple transcription units could potentially lead to instability and unequal cross-over during meiosis. As such, the donating laboratory strongly recommends maintaining this strain as heterozygous. When bred to mice expressing Cre recombinase, the offspring will have both STOP cassettes deleted in the cells where cre is expressed, resulting in sChroME*/GCaMP7s, mRuby3, and tTA2 expression. sChroME* is fused to a rat Kv2.1 potassium channel gene (Kcnb1) C-terminal sequence encoding a 65 amino acid sequence that functions to restrict protein localization to the soma and proximal dendrites. Specifically, the donating investigator reports Ai203 exhibits no visible sChroME*/GCaMP7s or mRuby3 fluorescence in the absence of cre. Of note, the Ai203 allele was designed with an IRES upstream of the mRuby3 and tTA2 to reduce/eliminate leakiness in the absence of Cre recombinase (Graybuck et al. 2021 Neuron [PMID:33789083]). The donating investigator reports when Ai203 mice are bred with Slc17a7-IRES2-Cre mice (Stock No. 037512) with cre expression in the cortex, olfactory bulb and anterior olfactory nuclei, mice exhibit robust native GCaMP7s expression in fixed brain tissue, with more widespread mRuby3 expression seen in the cortex. This may be due to selective silencing of the TREtight promoter relative to CAG which is more ubiquitous. When Ai203 mice are bred with Sst-IRES-cre mice (Stock No. 018973), wi"
