      "detailed_desc": "The design of these TIGRE2-jGCaMP8s-IRES-tTA2-WPRE mice was based on that of the Ai162 strain (PMID: 30007418; similar to Stock No. 031562). The expression of jGCaMP8s (a genetically encoded calcium indicator; GECI) and a tetracycline controlled transactivator (tTA2) is Cre recombinase‐dependent and under the regulation of the tetracycline‐responsive promoter element (TRE; tetO) that have been introduced into the intergenic Igs7 locus (also called TIGRE). The jGCaMP8s indicator is a fast rise, medium decay green fluorescent-based GECI with improved sensitivity and faster kinetics in targeted neuronal subpopulations. More information on the construct may be found in Nature&nbsp;615, 884&ndash;891 (2023), PMID: 36922596. Expression of tTA is attenuated by the introduction of an IRES (internal ribosome entry site) upstream of tTA. This modification ameliorates previously reported issues with overexpression of tTA. Offspring from pan‐excitatory and pan‐inhibitory crosses displayed no perinatal lethality, epileptiform activity, or signs of neurodegeneration. TIGRE2-jGCaMP8s-IRES-tTA2 mice (Stock No. 037119) additionally lack a downstream WPRE to further attenuate the expression of tTA. These mice were made by the Genetically-Encoded Neuronal Indicator and Effector (GENIE) Project at the HHMI's Janelia Farm Research Campus. 分子注记：The transgenic construct contains HS4 insulator-Tet response element/promoter (pTRE2)-loxP-Stop-loxP-CaMP8s-WPRE-pA-HS4 insulator-pCAG-lox2272-Stop-lox2272-FLAG-IRES-tTA2-WPRE-pA cassette was introduced to the Igs7 intergenic region. GCaMP8s (sensitive) incorporates a hexa-histidine affinity tag, an endothelial nitric oxide synthase peptide (ENOSP; modified with N19T, S24I, and S26M), a circularly permutated green fluorescent protein (cpGFP; modified with Q88E), the rat calcium-binding protein calmodulin (CaM; modified with F286Y and Q315H), and LKI amino acid linkers that replace the RS20 (previously referred to as M13) linkers."
