      "breeding_summary": "Mice homozygous for the Ank-G-GFP allele are fertile and may be used for breeding. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Ank3 (ankyrin 3, epithelial or AnkG) encodes an intracellular scaffolding protein and is expressed in the axonal initial segment (AIS) and nodes of Ranvier of neurons in the central and peripheral nervous systems. Ankyrin-G is critical for the formation and maintenance of the AIS. Ank-G-GFP knock-in mice were created using the flp excision system (FLEx) to insert an EGFP reporter fused to the last exon of Ank3 and downstream of the endogenous last exon of Ank3. The reporter is flanked by loxP/lox2272 sites. Upon exposure to Cre recombinase, the last exon-EGFP fusion is inverted, replacing the native last exon of Ank3 and transcribed allowing intrinsic labelling of Ankyrin-G. GFP expression does not interfere with normal structure or neuronal activity of the AIS. This strain may be used to visualize AIS modulation and plasticity in vitro (isolated cells, organotypic cultures, OTC), ex vivo (acute brain slices) and in vivo (live mice). 分子注记：The targeting vector is created using the flp excision system (FLEx). The vector contains from 5'; to 3': lox2272, loxP sites, a FLEx cassette containing the last exon of Ank3 (ENSMUSE00001264329 within ENSMUST00000182992.8), an FRT-flanked neo cassette, a pGHpA sequence, and an EGFP reporter in reverse orientation followed by lox2272 and loxP sites inserted downstream of the endogenous last exon"
