      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN1F5",
      "detailed_desc": "LumA knock-in reporter mice express a firefly (Photinus pyralis) luciferase gene with the R387X nonsense mutation that is inserted in to the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus, using CRISPR/Cas9 methodology. The R387X mutation eliminates the luciferase activity; however upon A-to-G correction by SpCas9 adenine base editors (ABEs), the enzymatic activity can be restored. Homozygous LumA mice are viable and fertile. The donating laboratory confirmed base editing in homozygous LumA mice by administering a single intravenous injection of ABEs encapsulated in lipid nanoparticles (LNPs). Their results indicated that luciferase activity was restored to 83% of wildtype in liver tissue and that the enzymatic activity was sustained for up to 4 months post injection as determined by whole body in vivo luminescence imaging. These LumA knock-in reporter mice may be a useful tool for evaluating new genome editing therapies, optimizing delivery methods and defining target tissue engagement. Five founders were obtained having germline transmission of the desired full-length Gt(ROSA)26Sor- LucR387X/T381T knock-in allele (LumA). Stock No. 038165 is LumA mice derived from male founder 9873 that were subsequently backcrossed to C57BL/6J one generation and cryopreserved as heterozygous sperm. The donating investigator reports their Yu et al., 2023 publication utilized LumA mice derived from female founder 9859 that were subsequently backcrossed to C57BL/6J for up to 5 generations. While no differences are anticipated, it should be noted that the phenotype of Stock No. 038165 could vary from that described in Yu et al., 2023. We will modify the strain description if necessary as published results become available. 分子注记：A guide RNA [5'- GCAGATCACGAGGGAAGAGG-3'] is selected to introduce a full-length luciferase gene, containing the R387X (c.A1159T) nonsense mutation and T381T silent mutation, into the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. The silent T381T mutation creates a new PAM site required for the binding of the base editor."
