      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, hemizygous mice may be bred to non-carrier littermates or C57BL/6J mice. Note that the donating laboratory has not attempted to produce homozygous transgenic mice to date (April 2023). Mating scheme: Hemizygote x Noncarrier; Noncarrier x Hemizygote Coat color: Black Generation: N10+pN2F4",
      "detailed_desc": "Neuromedin U receptors (NMUR) are a group of Gq/11-protein-coupled receptors that include two subtypes, NMUR1 and NMUR2, each coded by a unique gene (Nmur1 and Nmur2, respectively). NMUR1 is expressed in peripheral tissues while NMUR2 is expressed primarily in the central nervous system (CNS). In mice, NMUR1 expression was shown in a subset of innate lymphoid cells (ILC2) in intestinal and lung tissue. The endogenous ligands for these receptors, neuromedin U and neuromedin S, are neuropeptides produced by cholinergic neurons. Stimulation of NMUR1 by its ligand is believed to regulate multiple physiological processes including type 2 inflammation and tissue repair, as well as insulin secretion. Nmur1iCre-eGFP transgenic mice express an improved Cre recombinase (iCre) and an enhanced GFP (eGFP) under the control of the neuromedin U receptor 1 (Nmur1) promoter/enhancer elements (Tsou et al., Nature 2022). When these transgenic mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequences, Cre-recombinase activity is detected in Nmur1-expressing cells of the offspring. The Nmur1iCre-eGFP mice also express eGFP in Nmur1-expressing cells. Hemizygous Nmur1iCre-eGFP mice are viable and fertile with no overt phenotype. The donating laboratory has not attempted to produce homozygous Nmur1iCre-eGFP transgenic mice to date (April 2023). The donating investigator has indicated that eGFP expression is detectable by flow cytometry. Flow cytometry analysis completed by the donating laboratory confirmed eGFP expression in intestinal ILC2s with minimal to no expression observed in other immune cell populations. It was also found that eGFP expression was exclusive to ILC2s in both non-lymphoid and lymphoid tissues. The donating laboratory has also verified Cre-recombinase activity by crossing Nmur1iCre-eGFP to ROSA26iDTR mice (Stock No. 007900), which resulted in successful ablation of Nmur1-expressing ILC2s in the small intestine, colon, mesenteric lymph nodes (MLNs) and spleen after diphtheria toxin (DT) injection. These transgenic mice may be useful for studying the expression and function of Nmur1-expressing cells. Note that copy number and insertion site is not known for this Nmur1iCre-eGFP transgenic model to date (April 2023). 分子注记：The transgene was generated by replacing exons 2 and 3 of neuromedin U receptor 1 (Nmur1 gene), in the mouse BAC RP23-403I3, with a P2A-iCre-T2A-EGFP cassette followed by an FRT-flanked Kanamycin cassette. The FRT flanked kanamycin cassette was"
