      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous female mice may be bred to hemizygous male mice. Foxp3 is an X-linked gene. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Hemizygote Generation: N1+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "FOXP3 is a member of the forkhead transcription factor family and involved in regulatory T cell (Treg) differentiation and function. These Foxp3Ametrine-FlpO knock-in mice express an Ametrine reporter and an FlpO recombinase sequence under the direction of the forkhead box P3 (Foxp3) promoter/enhancer elements. The Ametrine reporter allows tracking of the regulatory T cells while the optimized Flp (FlpO) recombinase allows Treg cell-specific deletion of Frt-flanked genes. Homozygous female and hemizygous male Foxp3Ametrine-FlpO knock-in mice are viable and fertile with no overt phenotype. Ametrine expression can be measured by flow cytometry. When Foxp3Ametrine-FlpO mice are bred with mice containing FRT-flanked sequences, FlpO-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the FRT-flanked sequences in Foxp3-expressing cells in the offspring. The donating investigator bred these Foxp3Ametrine-FlpO mice to ThPOKF/F.iCreERT2.hCD2 transgenic mice (Stock No. 038538), to evaluate T cell subpopulations. Of the resulting progeny, those that were negative for iCre/ERT2 but positive for FlpO recombinase expressed the Ametrine reporter on Treg cells exclusively as expected. These Foxp3Ametrine-FlpO knock-in mice may be useful for T cell lineage tracing. 分子注记：An Ametrine-2A and FlpO (a codon-optimized flippase) cDNS followed by a 2A peptide linker was inserted after the ATG start codon of the Foxp3 gene with a AttB-Neo-AttP cassette. Germline mice were then crossed with Rosa.PhiC31 mice to remove the Neo cassette."
