      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygotes may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Generation: N5+pN1F5",
      "detailed_desc": "The Spp1 (secreted phosphoprotein 1, also known as osteopontin) gene encodes a glycoprotein with cytokine-like function originally described in bone that has more recently been identified as a potential neuroprotective target. Spp1 has been associated with microglia-synapse phagocytosis, especially as it relates to Alzheimer's disease (AD). Levels of secreted SPP1 are increased in cerebrospinal fluid and plasma in early AD and are correlated with cognitive decline. It is also a biomarker in some forms of cancer. SPP1 may therefore be of interest to researchers in the fields of bone growth/metabolism, cancer, and neurobiology. These B6.Spp1fl-EGFP-stop-tdTomato mutant mice possess loxP sites flanking flanking sequence encoding exons 4-7 of the secreted phosphoprotein 1 gene and an EGFP sequence with a stop cassette. They also contain a tdTomato with a stop cassette downstream of the 3&rsquo; loxP site. Mice that are homozygous for this allele are viable and fertile and have no overt phenotype. When these mutant mice are bred to mice that express Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have exons 4-7 and the EGFP-stop cassette deleted in the cre-expressing tissues. tdTomato expression is only evident after Cre excision of the floxed stop cassette and by direct fluorescence, immunofluorescence, and FACS. No SPP1 expression is detected in the tdTomato-positive cells after Cre recombination. 分子注记：The targeting vector is designed to contain (from 5' to 3';) a loxP site and a self-excising neomycin selection cassette placed upstream of exon 4, an enhanced green fluorescent protein sequence, a stop cassette, a second loxP site, and a tdTomato sequence with a stop cassette placed downstream of exon 7."
