      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygous and homozygous floxed mice are viable and fertile. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Exon 1 on the mouse ubiquinol-cytochrome c reductase, complex III subunit VI (Uqcrq) gene is flanked by loxP sites in these QPCfl mice. Cre recombinase-mediated excision of the floxed region results in loss of QPC protein and mitochondrial electron transport chain activity.Homozygous QPCfl mice are viable and fertile. Upon crossing with a cell or tissue specific cre-recombinase electron chain activity is reduced. This has been validated by a reduction in oxygen consumption in a variety of different cell types including regulatory T cell (Foxp3YFP-cre ,Stock No. 016959), endothelial cells (Cdh5-cre/ERT2), and macrophages (Lyz2-Cre, Stock No. 004781). 分子注记：A targeting vector was designed to insert a loxP site upstream of exon 1, and a FRT-flanked neomycin resistance (neo) cassette followed by a single loxP site downstream of exon 1 of the gene. Flp mediated recombination removed the neomycin cassette."
