      "breeding_summary": "Mice homozygous for both alleles are viable and fertile and can be used for mating. Mating scheme: Homozygous for Gt(ROSA)26Sortm1(rtTA*M2)Jae, Homozygous for&nbsp;Col1a1tm5(tetO-Cas9/Dntt*)Fcam x Homozygous for Gt(ROSA)26Sortm1(rtTA*M2)Jae, Homozygous for&nbsp;Col1a1tm5(tetO-Cas9/Dntt*)Fcam Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN1F5",
      "detailed_desc": "Cas9-TdT-gRNAs-M2 mice carry two targeted mutations: (1) a cas9 endonuclease fused to a mutant d138 terminal deoxynucleotidetransferase (Dntt, also known as Tdt) under the control of the a tetracycline responsive element (tetO or TRE) followed by ten tandem gRNAs driven by separate U6 promoters and (2) an optimized form of reverse tetracycline controlled transactivator (rtTA*M2) widely expressed from the Gt(ROSA)26Sor promoter. In this strain, administration of doxycycline induces widespread expression of cas9/Dntt which introduces site-directed double strand breaks in DNA through association with guide RNA. The Cas9-TdT-gRNAs-M2 allele represents an improvement over the KH2-iCas9 allele (Stock No. 029415) by incorporating a template-independent DNA polymerase (Dntt) that can insert random nucleotides at both overhang and blunt 3' ends. Co-expression of Cas9/Dntt generates a higher fraction of rare alleles and higher barcode diversity as compared to cas9 alone. To create the DARLIN model, Cas9-TdT-gRNAs-M2 mice are combined with CA/TA/RA triple target-array mice (B6;129S4-Gt(ROSA)26Sortm1(UBC-GFP)Fcam Igs7em1(CAG-mCherry)Fcam Col1a1tm4(CAG-EGFP)Fcam/J, Stock No. 038750). Administration of doxycycline to DARLIN mice activates expression of Cas9/Dntt allowing cut and repair of the target sequence creating a unique and inheritable \"barcode\". In comparison to the original CARLIN model (see Stock No. 035434), DARLIN can generate an estimated 1018 unique lineage barcodes and has 90% barcoding efficiency (compared to 30% in CARLIN). In single cell assays, 60% of captured cells have edited and rare lineage barcodes (10% in CARLIN). 分子注记：RMCE (recombinase-mediated cassette exchange) was utilized to insert the Cas9-Tdt (Dntt)-gRNA) construct into the Col1a1 locus. KH2 embryonic stem cells, carrying the Gt(ROSA)26Sor(tm1(rtTA*M2)Jae) allele, were previously re-targeted to insert an FRT-flanked PGK-Neo cassette and a promoterless hygromycin resistance cassette in the 3' UTR of the Col1a1 locus, thus adapting the ES cell line for RMCE. The Cas9-Dntt fusion is composed of the SpCas9 (derived from S. pyogenes) coding sequence (that includes an N-terminal 3xFLAG peptide, the SV40-NLS [nulcear localization sequence], and a C-terminal NLS), and the coding sequence of the mutant d138 Tdt (formal designation Dntt) containing an N-terminal 6xHis tag. The fusion was created by replacing the Cas9 stop codon with a linker sequence followed by the entire d138 Tdt coding sequence. "
