      "breeding_summary": "Mice homozygous for all three alleles are viable and fertile and can be used for mating. Mating scheme: Homozygous for Gt(ROSA)26Sortm1(UBC-EGFP)Fcam, Homozygous for Igs7em1(CAG-mCherry)Fcam, Homozygous for&nbsp;Col1a1tm4(CAG-EGFP)Fcam/J x&nbsp;Homozygous for Gt(ROSA)26Sortm1(UBC-EGFP)Fcam, Homozygous for Igs7em1(CAG-mCherry)Fcam, Homozygous for&nbsp;Col1a1tm4(CAG-EGFP)Fcam/J Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN1F4",
      "detailed_desc": "CA/TA/RA triple target-array knock-in mice carry three targeted mutations: (1) CA is an expression cassette containing 10 guide RNAs (gRNA) with separate U6 promoters, a CAG-driven GFP reporter in which the sequence targeted by the gRNAs is inserted upstream of its polyadenylation site and placed into the Col1a1 locus (2) TA has the same target sequences arranged into a different order and placed into the 3'UTR of CAG-mCherry reporter, the construct is inserted into the Igs7 locus, (3) RA has the same target sequences arranged into a different order and placed into the 3'UTR of a UBC-EGFP reporter and inserted into the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. The target sequences can be edited by the existing 10 tandem gRNAs inserted into the CA allele. To create the DARLIN model, CA/TA/RA triple target-array mice are combined with Cas9-TdT-gRNAs-M2 mice (B6;129S4-Gt(ROSA)26Sortm1(rtTA*M2)Jae Col1a1tm5(tetO-Cas9/Dntt*)Fcam/J, Stock No. 038749). Administration of doxycycline to DARLIN mice activates expression of Cas9/Dntt allowing cut and repair of the target sequence creating a unique and inheritable \"barcode\". DARLIN can generate an estimated 1018 unique lineage barcodes and has 60% of captured cells that have edited and rare lineage barcodes in single-cell assays. 分子注记：The targeting construct is designed as a multiplex containing 10 single guide RNAs (sgRNA) driven by separate U6 promoters inserted into the 3' UTR of an EGFP reporter driven by constitutive CAG promoter. A \"barcode\" 276 bp array containing target sites matching each of the expressed sgRNAs is inserted upstream of the EGFP polyadenylation site. The targeting construct construct contains a EGFP reporter with a WPRE, 10 target sites, an SV40-polyA signal, and 2xHS4 insulator elements inserted into the GFP 3Ã¢Â€Â™ UTR driven by a UBC (ubiquitin C) promoter and inserted in reverse orientation into the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. A \"barcode\" 276 bp array containing 10 target sites in a unique arrangement is inserted upstream of the EGFP polyadenylation site. The targeting construct contains the mCherry reporter open reading frame with a WPRE and the 10 target sequences (see below) inserted into the 3Ã¢Â€Â™ UTR driven by a CAG promoter and inserted into the Igs7 locus using CRISPR/cas9 genome editing. A \"barcode\" 276 bp array containing 10 target sites in a unique arrangement is inserted upstream of the EGFP polyadenylation site."
