      "breeding_summary": "Mice hemizygous for the transgene are viable and fertile. The donating investigator has not generated homozygotes. Mating scheme: Hemizygote x Noncarrier; Noncarrier x Hemizygote Generation: N10p+N3",
      "detailed_desc": "HSA-Cre-ERT2 mice express cre/ERT2 under control of the human skeletal muscle &alpha;-actin (ACTA1) promoter and regulatory elements (derived from a PAC). ACTA1 directs expression of the tamoxifen-inducible Cre recombinase to skeletal muscles. When transgenic mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked (floxed) sequences, tamoxifen-inducible cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of floxed sequences in transgene-expressing cells in the offspring. RT-PCR analysis confirms the presence of cre/ERT2 mRNA in fast (quadriceps, gastrocnemius), mixed (tibialis), and slow (soleus) muscles, but not in heart or any other tissue tested. Immunohistochemical analysis demonstrates cre protein expression in 50% of nuclei of skeletal muscles. Cre/ERT2 provides a higher efficiency of recombination than Cre/ER and can be induced by a milder tamoxifen treatment (0.1 mg for 5 days). Hemizygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported phenotype abnormalities. The donating investigator did not attempt to make a homozygous colony, it is unknown if homozygotes are viable and fertile. The Cre-ERT2 fusion protein consists of Cre recombinase fused to a triple mutant form of the human estrogen receptor which does not bind its natural ligand (17&beta;-estradiol) at physiological concentrations but will bind the synthetic estrogen receptor ligands 4-hydroxytamoxifen (OHT or tamoxifen) and, with lesser sensitivity, ICI 182780. Restricted to the cytoplasm, Cre-ERT2 can only gain access to the nuclear compartment after exposure to tamoxifen. To counteract the mixed estrogen agonist effects of tamoxifen injections, which can result in late fetal abortions in pregnant mice, progesterone may be coadministered. 分子注记：Tamoxifen-dependent Cre-ERT2 recombinase cDNA was inserted at the human skeletal alpha-actin (ACTA1) transcriptional initiation codon in exon 2 of a 90-kb HSA genomic segment contained in a PAC. Five copies were integrated into the genome in this line."
