      "detailed_desc": "These TIGRE2-RiboL1-jGCaMP8s-IRES-tTA2 mice (described on the Janelia Research Campus website) are similar to STOCK Igs7tm2(tetO-GCaMP8s,CAG-tTA2)Genie/J animals (Stock No. 037719). They co-express a fusion of jGCaMP8s genetically encoded calcium indicator (GECI) tethered to a component of the large ribosomal subunit (Rpl10) via an optimized linker sequence (L1) and a tetracycline-controlled transactivator (tTA2) in a Cre recombinase-dependent manner from the intergenic Igs7 (TIGRE) locus. By tethering jGCaMP8s to the ribosome, protein expression is restricted to the cell soma thereby reducing neuropil signals. The expression of this improved jGCaMP8s (a genetically encoded calcium indicator; GECI) and a tetracycline controlled tetracycline controlled transactivator (tTA2) is Cre recombinase‐dependent and under the regulation of the tetracycline‐responsive promoter element (TRE; tetO) that have been introduced to the intergenic Igs7 locus (also called TIGRE). The jGCaMP8s indicator is a fast rise, medium decay green fluorescent-based GECI with improved sensitivity and faster kinetics in targeted neuronal subpopulations. Expression of tTA is attenuated by the introduction of an IRES (internal ribosome entry site) upstream of tTA and the omission of a WPRE enhancer element downstream. These modifications ameliorate previously reported issues with overexpression of tTA. Offspring from pan‐excitatory and pan‐inhibitory crosses displayed no perinatal lethality, epileptiform activity, or signs of neurodegeneration. These mice were made by the Genetically-Encoded Neuronal Indicator and Effector (GENIE) Project at the HHMI's Janelia Farm Research Campus. 分子注记：The transgenic construct contains an HS4 insulator-Tet response element/promoter (pTRE2)-loxP-Stop-loxP-RiboL1-CaMP8s-WPRE-pA-HS4 insulator-pCAG-lox2272-Stop-lox2272-FLAG-IRES-tTA2-pA cassette introduced to the Igs7 intergenic region. RiboL1 is a ribo-tag sequence modified from Rpl10, ribosomal protein L10. gCaMP8s (sensitive) incorporates a hexa-histidine affinity tag, an endothelial nitric oxide synthase peptide (ENOSP; modified with N19T, S24I, and S26M), a circularly permutated green fluorescent protein (cpGFP; modified with Q88E), the rat calcium-binding protein calmodulin (CaM; modified with F286Y and Q315H), and LKI amino acid linkers that replace the RS20 (previously referred to as M13) linkers."
