      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: F4pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Apoe (apoliprotein E) encodes a fat-binding protein involved in lipoprotein metabolism and cardiovascular disease. It is involved in the transport of fats, fat-soluble vitamins, and cholesterol into the lymph system and variants in human APOE have been associated with increased risk of Alzheimer's disease (AD). The human APOE*R136S variant was first reported in a human patient with type III hyperlipoproteinemia by a group at Christchurch Hospital in New Zealand. The R136S variant is at a border of a region of APOE involved in binding to lipoprotein receptors and heparan sulfate proteoglycans (HSPGs). HSPGs have been suggested to promote amyloid-&Beta; aggregation and neuronal uptake of extracellular Tau, and APOE binding may be necessary for some of these effects. A patient who carried early onset AD (EOAD)-risk allele, PSEN1*E280A, and was homozygous for this human SNP rs121918393, found in human APOE mature protein, exhibited resilience to a high central nervous system (CNS) amyloid load. To produce the Apoe*R136S allele, CRISPR/Cas9 endonuclease-mediated genome editing was used to introduce a CGG to TCT missense mutation resulting in an arginine to serine mutation (R128S) in the apolipoprotein E (Apoe) gene. RNA-seq analysis of hippocampus and cortex indicates that the Apoe*R136S allele is expressed at a level similar to the wild-type APOE allele, with no evidence of cryptic splicing products from the mutant allele. If additional characterization of these Apoe*R136S mice is performed, we may modify the strain description accordingly. Both heterozygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile. 分子注记：Using CRISPR/Cas9 technology, a guide RNA (gcacagaggagatacgggcg) was designed to produce a CGG to TCT missense mutation resulting in an arginine to serine mutation (R128S) in the apolipoprotein E (Apoe) gene. The missense mutation corresponds to the human SNP rs121918393 found in human APOE mature protein and is associated with an increased risk of AlzheimerÃ¢Â€Â™s disease (AD)."
