      "breeding_summary": "Homozygous mice are viable with no gross abnormalities and normal fertility. When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote",
      "detailed_desc": "The Olfr558 KO mice have loxP::frt::PGK-neo(STOP)::frt::TetO::loxP inserted just upstream of the start ATG of the Or51e1 locus. It's a knock-out (KO) first before Cre recombination. Cre recombination rescues the Or51e1 expression. Also, it can be used for Tet-controllable ectopic expression (before FLP), and after FLP, Tet-controllable Or51e1 overexpression with tTA or knockdown/KO with tTS [Tanaka et al., Biol Psychiatry 67:770]. Olfactory receptor 558 (OLFR558) is one of only three mammalian ORs to have been well-conserved by evolution in mammals, including mice, rats and human. In addition to act in the olfactory epithelium (OE) to mediate the sense of smell, it is expressed in murine kidney and localizes to renin-positive cells in the kidney and to vascular smooth muscle cells where its role was largely unknown. The donating investigator's report confirms the absence of Or51e1 mRNA in the kidney, blood vessels, heart, and BAT in homozygous KO mice where Olfr558 is normally expressed. Both male and female homozygous mice are viable and fertile but show an absence of physiological blood pressure sex differences in 10-week-old mice. Female KOs exhibit increased blood pressure and increased pulse wave velocity. In contrast, male KO mice have decreased renin expression and activity, altered vascular reactivity, and decreased diastolic pressure. There were no mechanical properties differences in blood vessels between KO and WT. Of note, the donating investigator has donated floxed Olfr78 conditional knockout mice (Stock No. 039290). Olfr78 is also expressed in a subset of vascular cells in renal blood vessels. This line will be useful for studies of the tissue-specific functions of Olfr558. 分子注记：Flexible Accelerated STOP Tetracycline Operator (tetO)-knockin (FAST) was used to insert a construct containing a loxP site, FRT site, neo cassette, STOP, FRT site, tetracycline operator (tetO) and loxP site upstream of the translation initiation site."
