      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Hbo1lox mice have loxP sites flanking exon 1 of the K(lysine) acetyltransferase 7 (Kat7) gene. Hbo1 encodes a histone 3 lysine 14 (H3K14) acetyltransferase which is involved in DNA replication, gene transcription, proliferation, cell fate commitment, and differentiation in the developing brain and neural stem and progenitor cells (NSPCs). HBO1 is essential for the maintenance of hematopoietic stem cells. Homozygous mice are viable and fertile. When bred to nestin-cre transgenic mice (Stock No. 003771), deletion in NSPCs results in the loss of H3K14 acetylation and failure of NSPCs to differentiate into neurons and oligodendrocytes. This deletion also abrogates neural stem cell plasticity, diverse differentiation pathways, and cerebral cortex development. These mice may be useful when studying the role of KAT7 in the activation of the neuronal and oligodendrocytic gene expression programs as well as in hematopoiesis. The donating investigator has deposited a group of floxed strains that are useful for studying development of hematopoietic stem cells and the regulation of hematopoiesis: Kat6afl [Moz3lox] (Stock No. 039488) Phf6lox (Stock No. 039489) Kat7lox [Hbo1lox] (Stock No. 039490) Ing5fl (Stock No. 039502) Ing4fl (Stock No. 039503) 分子注记：A loxP site was inserted upstream of exon 1. An FRT-flanked neo cassette with a 3' loxP site was inserted downstream of exon 1. Flp-mediated recombination removed the neo cassette leaving exon 1 floxed."
