      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes and homozygotes are viable and fertile. Generation: ?+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Adra2aT2a-CreER knock-in mice express tamoxifen-inducible cre recombinase from the mouse adrenergic receptor, alpha 2a (Adra2a) promoter enabling the excision of loxP-flanked sequences in Adra2a-expressing cells, including dorsal root ganglion (DRG) neurons and sympathetic neurons. DRG neurons labeled using the Adra2aT2a-CreER (CGRP-&gamma;+ subtype) allele in combination with the Brn3acKOAP allele (Pou4f1flox; Stock No. 010558) show restricted labeling in the lower thoracic and L6-S1 level. Little to no axonal labeling is observed in the skin of the limbs and trunk in these mice; however, robust labeling of terminals in internal organs, including the bladder and colon, has been observed. Thus, CGRP-&gamma; neurons have been shown to selectively innervate internal organs but not skin. It is unknown whether there is expression of this allele in the central nervous system. Expression of the targeted Adra2a gene is not disrupted. Homozygotes are viable and fertile and demonstrate no overt phenotype. 分子注记：The T2a-cre/ERT2 cassette followed by STOP and frt flanked neo cassette was inserted directly upstream of the stop codon in the last exon of the Adra2a gene."
