      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Rosa26-OsTir1-F74Gflox knock-in (KI) mice were developed to express the Japanese rice Oryza sativa F-box transport inhibitor response 1 (TIR1, formal name LOC4337827) protein, harboring the F74G modification, for use in the second generation auxin-inducible degron (AID2) system for rapid and reversible degradation of auxin inducible degron-tagged (AID) proteins. TIR1 interacts with the mouse Cullin-RING ubiquitin ligase complex and an AID-targeted protein. Following addition of the auxin derivative 5-Ph-IAA, the target protein is degraded by the proteasome. A CAG promoter directs expression of a c-Myc (Myc) tagged TIR1F74G sequence from the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. Homozygous Rosa26-OsTir1-F74Gflox mice are viable and fertile. When bred to mice that express tissue-specific Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have TIR1-F74G expressed in the cre-expressing tissues. The donating laboratory confirmed expression of TIR1-F74G across various tissues, after crossing these mice to a Sox2Cre mouse line (Stock No. 008454), with the lowest expression detected in the brain and kidney. These mice may be a valuable tool for studying protein function. 分子注记：Using CRISPR/Cas9 technology, single guide RNA [5'-actccagtctttctagaaga-3'] was used to introduce a CMV-IE enhancer/chicken beta-actin/rabbit beta-globin hybrid promoter (CAG), a loxP-flanked STOP cassette including a puromycin cassette, the codon-optimized Oryza sativa F-box transport inhibitor response 1 (TIR1) sequence harboring the F74G modification and a c-myc (Myc) epitope tag, into intron 1 of the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus on chromosome 6."
