      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Sox6fl/fl mice have loxP sites flanking coding exon two (CE2) of the SRY (sex determining region Y)-box 6 (Sox6) gene. Cre recombinase-mediated removal of CE2 results in a null allele (Sox6-) because splicing of CE1 into CE3 or CE4 creates a frameshift followed by a stop codon. The resulting transcript encodes a short protein lacking the main functional domains of SOX6 (homodimerization domains and DNA-binding domain) and likely undergoes premature decay. Sox6 encodes a transcription factor involved in the lineage determination and differentiation of discrete cell types from embryonic development onto adulthood. These cell types include chondrocytes, interneurons, and skeletal and cardiac muscle cells. Sox6fl/fl mice are viable, look normal throughout life, and are fertile. Recombination of Sox6fl in the germline of males harboring a PrmCre transgene (Stock No. 003328) results in progeny containing a Sox6- allele. Sox6+/- mice are viable, look normal throughout life and are fertile, whereas Sox6-/- mice fail to thrive in the neonatal period and die by weaning age, likely due to neurodevelopmental, cardiac and skeletal muscle defects. They also show mild skeletal defects, including a kinky tail. Sox6fl/fl mice carrying a Prx1Cre transgene (Stock No. 005584), which recombines Sox6fl in early limb bud mesenchymal cells and some sternum progenitor cells, have slightly smaller limbs and a shorter sternum than wildtype littermates, but look otherwise normal and are viable and fertile. The same is true for Sox5fl/fl mice (Stock No. 039620) carrying Prx1Cre. However, due to redundancy of Sox5 and Sox6 in chondrogenesis, Sox5fl/flSox6fl/flPrx1Cre mice are born with very small and malformed limbs and a rudimentary sternum. Unable to ambulate properly, these mice need to be euthanized before they reach weaning age. 分子注记：Exon 2 was flanked by a single loxP site and an frt flanked neo cassette followed by a single loxP site. Flp mediated recombination then removed the neo cassette."
