      "detailed_desc": "These Ai63(TIT-tdT)-D mice (also called Ai63) are a fluorescent Tet reporter line, created by targeted insertion at the Igs7 locus (TIGRE; an intergenic region on mouse chromosome 9 that allows reporter expression to be tightly regulated). Ai63 mice harbor the TIGRE-Ins-TRE-tdTomato allele designed with a modified Tet response element (TRE or tetO) upstream of the tdTomato fluorescent protein. When bred with other mice expressing tetracycline-controlled transactivator protein (tTA) and/or reverse tetracycline-controlled transactivator protein (rtTA), tdTomato expression in cells/tissues, where tTA/rtTA is expressed, can regulated with tetracycline or its analog doxycycline (dox). This line was created by a germline deletion of the floxed-STOP cassette from the related strain Ai62(TITL-tdTomato) (Stock No. 022731). Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile with no reported gross physical or behavioral abnormalities. The donating investigator reports Ai63 mice have no reported levels of tdTomato expression in absence of tTA. In the cells expressing tTA, tdTomato expression may be detected by direct/native fluorescence and by in situ hybridization (using a tdTomato probe sequence) after doxycycline administration. When bred to Rorb-T2A-tTA2 mice (Stock No. 028537), robust native tdTomato expression is evident in cortical layer 4. Homozygous mice are viable and fertile. 分子注记：The targeting constructed introduced by recombinase mediated cassette exchange at the existing site inserted anan FRT3 site, two tandem copies of the chicken beta-globin HS4 insulator element (to reduce expression of the reporter gene in the absence of transactivator protein), a modified Tet response element (TRE or (tetO); described in detail below), a loxP-flanked STOP cassette (with stop codons in all three reading frames linked to a synthetic pA-hGHpA-PGKpA unit), a sequence encoding the tdTomato fluorescent protein (a non-oligomerizing DsRed fluorescent protein variant with a 12 residue linker fusing two copies of the protein (tandem dimer)), a woodchuck hepatitis virus post-transcriptional regulatory element (WPRE; to enhance the mRNA transcript stability), a bovine growth hormone polyA signal, two tandem copies of the chicken beta-globin HS4 insulator element, an AttB site, a PGK-5'hygro cassette, an RNA splice donor and a FRT5 site. PhiC31-mediated recombination removed the hygromycin cassette and replaced it with the recombined AttB/AttP site (AttL). Mating with cre recombinase mic"
