      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, double homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygous for Nr1h3tm1.1Gust, Heterozygous for&nbsp;Nr1h2tm1.1Gust x&nbsp;Heterozygous for&nbsp;Nr1h3tm1.1Gust, Heterozygous for&nbsp;Nr1h2tm1.1Gust Coat color: Black Generation: N3p+F0",
      "detailed_desc": "LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice have loxP sites flanking exons 4-6 of the nuclear receptor subfamily 1, group H, member 3 (Nr1h3; LXR&alpha;) gene (on Chromosome 2) and loxP sites flanking exons 5-7 of the nuclear receptor subfamily 1, group H, member 2 (Nr1h2; LXR&beta;) gene (on Chromosome 7). Double homozygous LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice are viable and fertile. Nr1h3 and Nr1h2 encode Liver X Receptors (LXRs) LXR&alpha; and LXR&beta;, respectively. They are nuclear receptors that regulate macrophage function by controlling transcriptional programs involved in lipid homeostasis and inflammation. Specifically, LXR&alpha; and LXR&beta; sense intracellular oxysterols and intermediates of the cholesterol biosynthetic pathway and regulate expression of genes involved in reverse cholesterol transport, fatty acid synthesis, and immune function. LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl double floxed mice are viable and fertile when homozygous for both mutations, and they exhibit normal expression of both targeted genes prior to cre exposure. Whole-body LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;-/- knock-out mice exhibit cholesterol accumulation in the thymus, accelerated thymic involution, and impaired T cell development. When LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice with are bred with thymic epithelial cell (TEC)-specific Foxn1ex9cre mice (Stock No. 018448), resulting FoxN1-LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice exhibit thymic involution after dexamethasone-induction, and modest effects on the activation state of T cells. When LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice with are bred with T lymphocyte-specific Lck-Cre mice (Stock No. 003802), resulting Lck-LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice exhibit lower frequencies of single positive thymocytes and peripheral T cells. When LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice with are bred with macrophage-specific Csf1rCre mice (Stock No. 029206), resulting Csf1r-LXR&alpha;fl/fl&beta;fl/fl mice exhibit thymic lipid accumulation and resistance to acute thymic involution after dexamethasone-induction. 分子注记：A loxP site in intron 4, frt and loxP sites in intron 7 are inserted into the Nr1h2 gene. A loxP site in intron 3, frt and loxP sites in intron 4, and a third loxP site in intron 6 were inserted into the Nr1h3 gene."
