      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N20+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Tg.Sirt6 mice contain a Cre-inducible knock-in of the mouse sirtuin 6 (Sirt6) cDNA with a C-terminal single FLAG tag introduced to the Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. A floxed Neo/STOP cassette prevents FLAG-Sirt6 expression in the absence of Cre recombinase. After removal of the loxP-flanked STOP cassette, FLAG-SIRT6 is produced in Cre-expressing cells and daughter cells. Sirt6 encodes a lysine deacylase of histones and non-histone proteins. It is implicated in the regulation of many key cellular processes such as metbolism homeostasis, immunity, inflammation, and genomic stability. Tg.Sirt6 mice are viable and fertile. Breeding females with male Pgk1-Cre mice (Stock No. 020811), results in whole-body FLAG-Sirt6-overexpressing mice. These mice are useful for studying effect of tissue-specific overexpression of SIRT6 in various pathophysiologic conditions. 分子注记：The targeting vector was designed to insert the Sirt6-FLAG cDNA into the Gt(ROSA)26Sor driven by its promoter and controlled by a STOP cassette. The STOP cassette in the vector consisted of a splice acceptor and the floxed (PGK)/gb2neoPGKpolyA2xSV40pA sequence and was inserted in intron 1 of ROSA26 locus. Mouse Sirt6 cDNA with a C-terminal FLAG tag was cloned immediately downstream of the STOP cassette. The Sirt6-FLAG sequence was followed by a BGHpA bovine growth hormone polyadenylation (BGHpA) sequence."
