      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: ?+pN2F1",
      "detailed_desc": "CXCL9 (also known as MIG, monokine induced by gamma-interferon) and CXCL10 (IP-10, interferon-induced protein of 10kDa) are ligands for the C-X-C motif chemokine receptor 3 (CXCR3). CXCR3 is highly expressed on T cells and natural killer cells and plays an important role in immune cell trafficking, immune responses and inflammatory processes. The REX3 (Reporting the Expression of CXCR3 ligands) transgenic mouse line co-expresses a red fluorescent protein (RFP) driven by the mouse C-X-C motif chemokine ligand 9 (Cxcl9) promotor and a blue fluorescent protein (BFP) driven by the mouse C-X-C motif chemokine ligand 10 (Cxcl10) promoter. Hemizygous and homozygous mice are viable and fertile. RFP and BFP expression is detectable by flow cytometry. These mice may be useful for tracking the cellular source of CXCL9 and CXCL10 chemokine expression in immune response and inflammatory pathways. Of note, the transgene integration site and copy number have not been confirmed by the donating laboratory. 分子注记：A BAC clone containing the Cxcl9 and Cxcl10 genes was altered by the insertion of a RFP and BFP gene into the ATG start site of the Cxcl9 and Cxcl10 genes, respectively. Transgenic mice carrying the construct express the spectrally distinct fluorescent reporter proteins which report the expression of the CXCR3 ligands."
