      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes are viable and fertile. Homozygotes are born in reduced numbers and survivors are reported to live a maximum of 10 weeks on an FVB genetic background. The donating laboratory maintained this strain through heterozygote x FVB/NHanHsd crosses. The donating laboratory wishes to note: Important - Experiments with this mouse strain should only be performed in homozygotes on a C57BL/6-FVB F1 background, which gives homozygotes in approximately Mendelian ratio&rsquo;s. Many laboratories study these mice in this specific background, making study comparison possible. Please contact the donating laboratory for details. Coat color: Albino Generation: N75+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Ercc1- mice carry a targeted knock-out of the mouse Ercc1 (excision repair cross-complementing rodent repair deficiency, complementation group 1) gene. A neomycin cassette was introduced to the last coding exon (exon 7), preventing the expression of 74 essential carboxy terminal amino acids. Expression analysis shows an absence of transcript in mouse embryonic fibroblasts derived from homozygous mutant mice. Ercc1- homozygotes demonstrate retarded growth, enlarged liver nuclei, and greatly reduced lifespan (3-8 weeks). Homozygotes are born in reduced numbers (many dying by embryonic day 13.5) when bred on a pure C57BL/6 or FVB background. Therefore, experimental animals were only bred on a C57BL/6-FVB F1 genetic background by the donating laboratory. They exhibit an absence of subcutaneous fat, early onset of ferritin deposition in the spleen, kidney malfunction, gross abnormalities of ploidy, and cytoplasmic invaginations in nuclei of liver and kidney, and compromised nucleotide excision repair (NER) and cross-link repair. In addition, ERCC1-mutant cells undergo premature replicative senescence. Heterozygotes are not known to exhibit any phenotype. (Weeda, 1997; PMID 9197240) This mutation is also available on a predominantly C57BL/6-backcrossed genetic background (see Stock No. 040162), with homozygous animals reportedly surviving up to 38 days. The donating laboratory wishes to note that all of their compound mutant experiments (PMID 27556946, PMID 36756698, PMID 38498063, PMID 22953029, PMID 38689513, PMID 38451018) were performed on an F1 hybrid genetic background. This hybrid background was derived from crosses of C57BL/6JOlaHsd-background mutant animals with FVB/NHanHsd-background mutant animals (e.g. Ercc1+/- FVB x Ercc1d/+C57BL/6 (Stock No. 040165)). The contributing single mutant alleles were maintained independently through crosses of heterozygotes with C57BL/6JOlaHsd or FVB/NHanHsd inbred mice rather than wildtype animals from within their colonies (e.g. Ercc1-/+ FVB x WT (Ercc1+/+) FVB). They did not maintain homozygous colonies and their F1 mice were not further intercrossed. 分子注记：Exon 7 was disrupted by the insertion of a neomycin selection cassette. Expression analysis showed an absence of transcript in mouse embryonic fibroblasts derived from homozygous mutant mice. Further analysis showed that transcription of the antisense gene was unaffected by the targeting event."
