      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes are viable and fertile. Homozygotes are born in reduced numbers (many dying by embryonic day 13.5) and show severe runting. Although some homozygotes survive to 6 months of age on the C57BL/6 genetic background, they are believed to be infertile. The donating laboratory maintained this strain through heterozygote x C57BL/6JOlaHsd crosses. The donating laboratory wishes to note: Important - Experiments with this mouse strain should only be performed in homozygotes on a C57BL/6-FVB F1 background, which gives homozygotes in approximately Mendelian ratio&rsquo;s. Many laboratories study these mice in this specific background, making study comparison possible. Please contact the donating laboratory for details. Generation: N75+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "ERCC1*292 (also called Ercc1delta or Ercc1d) mice demonstrate a partial inactivation of the mouse Ercc1 (excision repair cross-complementing rodent repair deficiency, complementation group 1) gene. A neomycin cassette was introduced to intron 9 and a TAG stop codon and diagnostic BamHI restriction site were created in exon 10, preventing the expression of the last 7 amino acids (two of which are in the ERCC1 essential domain). Transcription, at levels that are approximately 15% that of wildtype, and mRNA processing remain intact. Neomycin is excluded from the protein product by splicing. The encoded stable protein terminates immediately after the Escherichia coli nucleotide excision repair (NER) endonuclease UvrC-homologous region. Transcription of an overlapping antisense gene (Polr1g; also called Ase1) is unaffected by the Ercc1 targeting event. ERCC1*292 (Ercc1d) homozygotes are born in reduced numbers (many dying by embryonic day 13.5) when bred in a pure C57BL/6 or FVB background and show retarded growth. Therefore, experimental animals were only bred on a C57BL/6-FVB F1 genetic background by the donating laboratory. On a C57BL/6 genetic background, homozygotes are reported to have a life span of up to 6 months. Ercc1d/- mice (Ercc1d x Ercc1- (Stock No. 040163)) exhibit an absence of subcutaneous fat, early onset of ferritin deposition in the spleen, kidney malfunction, nuclear abnormalities in the kidney and liver, neurodegeneration and cardiovascular aging, and compromised nucleotide excision repair (NER). Mouse embryonic fibroblasts (MEFs) derived from homozygotes grow three times more slowly than wildtype fibroblasts in vitro. (Weeda, 1997; PMID 9197240) ERCC1*292 heterozygotes on a mixed FVB:C57BL/6J genetic background demonstrate decreased striatal dopaminergic innervation in the caudate putamen, paralleled by increased tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) expression in substantia nigra pars compacta (SNpc) neuronal bodies. (PMID 27210754, Fig. 2) This mutation is also available on a predominantly FVB genetic background (see Stock No. 040165), with homozygous animals reportedly surviving up to ~78 days. The donating laboratory wishes to note that all of their ERCC1*292 (Ercc1delta, Ercc1d) compound mutant experiments (PMID 27556946, PMID 36756698, PMID 38498063, PMID 22953029, PMID 38689513, PMID 38451018) were performed on an F1 hybrid genetic background. This hybrid background was derived from crosses of C57BL/6JOlaHsd-background mutant animals with FVB/"
