      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes are viable and fertile. Homozygotes are reported to die by ~78 days of age on the FVB genetic background. The donating laboratory maintained this strain through heterozygote x FVB/NHanHsd crosses. The donating laboratory wishes to note: Important - Experiments with this mouse strain should only be performed in homozygotes on a C57BL/6-FVB F1 background, which gives homozygotes in approximately Mendelian ratio&rsquo;s. Many laboratories study these mice in this specific background, making study comparison possible. Please contact the donating laboratory for details. Coat color: Albino Generation: N75F1",
      "detailed_desc": "ERCC1*292 (also called Ercc1delta or Ercc1d) mice demonstrate a partial inactivation of the mouse Ercc1 (excision repair cross-complementing rodent repair deficiency, complementation group 1) gene. A neomycin cassette was introduced to intron 9 and a TAG stop codon and diagnostic BamHI restriction site were created in exon 10, preventing the expression of the last 7 amino acids (two of which are in the ERCC1 essential domain). Transcription, at levels that are approximately 15% that of wildtype, and mRNA processing remain intact. Neomycin is excluded from the protein product by splicing. The encoded stable protein terminates immediately after the Escherichia coli nucleotide excision repair (NER) endonuclease UvrC-homologous region. Transcription of an overlapping antisense gene (Polr1g; also called Ase1) is unaffected by the Ercc1 targeting event. ERCC1*292 (Ercc1d) homozygotes are born in reduced numbers (many dying sometime after embryonic day 13.5) when bred in a pure C57BL/6 or FVB background and show retarded growth. Therefore, experimental animals were only bred on a C57BL/6-FVB F1 genetic background by the donating laboratory. On this FVB genetic background, homozygotes are reported to have a life span of up to ~78 days. (Weeda, 1997; PMID 9197240) ERCC1*292 (Ercc1d) heterozygotes on a mixed FVB:C57BL/6J genetic background demonstrate decreased striatal dopaminergic innervation in the caudate putamen, paralleled by increased tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) expression in substantia nigra pars compacta (SNpc) neuronal bodies. (PMID 27210754, Fig. 2) This mutation is also available on a predominantly C57BL/6 genetic background (see Stock No. 040164), with homozygous animals reportedly surviving up to ~6 months. The donating laboratory wishes to note that all of their ERCC1*292 (Ercc1delta, Ercc1d) compound mutant experiments (PMID 27556946, PMID 36756698, PMID 38498063, PMID 22953029, PMID 38689513, PMID 38451018) were performed on an F1 hybrid genetic background. This hybrid background was derived from crosses of C57BL/6JOlaHsd-background mutant animals with FVB/NHanHsd-background mutant animals (e.g. Ercc1+/- C57BL/6 (Stock No. 040162) x Ercc1d/+ FVB). The contributing single mutant alleles were maintained independently through crosses of heterozygotes with C57BL/6JOlaHsd or FVB/NHanHsd inbred mice rather than wildtype animals from within their colonies (e.g. Ercc1d/+ FVB x WT (Ercc1+/+) FVB). They did not maintain homozygous colonies and their F1 mice wer"
