      "breeding_summary": "Heterozygotes are viable and fertile. The donating laboratory maintained this strain through crosses of C57BL/6J females (Stock No. 000664) with DAT-FlpO heterozygous males. The viability/fertility of homozygotes was not assessed by their group. (January, 2025) Update September, 2025 - Crosses of heterozygous mice produce homozygotes that are significantly smaller than wildtype and heterozygous animals. We are now assessing their fertility. Mating scheme: +/+ sibling x Heterozygote; Heterozygote x +/+ sibling Generation: N10+pN2",
      "detailed_desc": "In Parkinson's disease, dopaminergic neurons (DANs) in the midbrain gradually degenerate, with ventral substantia nigra pars compacta (SNc) DANs exhibiting greater vulnerability. Slc6a3 (solute carrier family 6 (neurotransmitter transporter, dopamine), member 3; also called DAT) encodes a dopamine transporter protein and is expressed in dopaminergic neurons. DAT-FlpO (also called DAT-Flp or Slc6a3-T2A-FlpO) mice express optimized Flp recombinase (FlpO) from the mouse Slc6a3 promoter. Expression of the targeted gene is not disrupted by the knock-in mutation. Heterozygous mice demonstrate no overt phenotype and are fertile. When crossed with animals carrying FRT-flanked sequences, the FRT'ed region is excised in Slc6a3-expressing cells of the offspring. Characterization of the DAT-FlpO line expression and examination of whole-brain efferent and afferent connectivity of dopaminergic neuron subtypes was accomplished through crosses with an unspecified Ai65 Flp reporter line. TdTomato+ cells were confirmed to be tyrosine hydroxylase positive (TH+) neurons. (Fushiki, 2024; PMID 39763754) 分子注记：The TAA stop codon in exon 15 of the mouse Slc6a3 gene on mouse Chromosome 13 was replaced with a T2A-FlpO-rBG (rabbit beta-globin polyadenylation signal)-pA cassette using CRISPR/cas9 methodologies."
