      "detailed_desc": "This mouse line is a C57BL/6J congenic strain that carries the differential Ptprca pan leukocyte marker, commonly known as CD45.1 or Ly5.1, that is used widely in transplant studies (see Stock No. 002014). It also carries the OT-1 transgene that contains mouse Tcra-V2 and Tcrb-V5 genes (see Stock No. 003831). This transgenic T cell receptor was designed to recognize ovalbumin peptide residues 257-264 (OVA257-264) in the context of H2Kb (CD8 co-receptor interaction with MHC class I). This results in MHC class I-restricted, ovalbumin-specific, CD8+ T cells (OT-I cells) used to study CD8+ T cell response to antigen, positive selection, and in any research requiring CD8+ T cells of defined specificity. Mice also contain a Rosa26-Cas9 knock-in allele that constitutively express CRISPR associated protein 9 (Cas9) endonuclease and EGFP in a widespread fashion under the direction of a CAG promoter (similar to Stock No. 026179). When used in combination with single guide RNAs, the Rosa26-Cas9 allele allows for editing of single or multiple mouse genes. This mutant mouse line is useful for tracking gene knock-out CD8+ T cell responses in vivo or ex vivo. Due to the presence of the OT-1 transgene, there is a significant increase in the number of CD8+ T cells, all with a defined antigen specificity. The donating investigator has made other similar mouse lines available including P14 CD45.1 Cas9 mice (Stock No. 040736) and OT-2 CD45.1 Cas9 mice (Stock No. 040737). 分子注记：Transgenic mice carry two coinjected constructs containing rearranged mouse TCR alpha (Tcra-V2, Tcra-J(alpha26)) and TCR beta (Tcrb-V5, Tcrb-D(beta2), Tcrb-J(beta2.6)) chains isolated from T cell clone 149.42. This transgenic T cell receptor recognizes ovalbumin residues 257-264 (SIINFEKL) in the context of H2Kb. The rearranged Tcra (alpha chain) cDNA specific for ovalbumin was isolated from T cells (clone AD10) and is expressed under the control of a 2-kb fragment of the H-2Kb promoter, a 700-bp fragment including the Ig H chain enhancer located 5' to the promoter, and a 1.7-kb BamHI-PstI fragment containing the 3' half of the human adult 8-globin gene (including part of exon 2, the exon 2-exon 3 C.F6 TCR a-chain gene that was truncated at the 3' XbaI site intron, exon 3) and polyadenylation signal. The Tcrb (beta chain) construct consists of a genomic fragment containing the Tcrb coding and endogenous promoter regions from a T cell clone (B3) specific for ovalbumin. The Pepc gene controls electrophoret"
