      "breeding_summary": "The donating investigator has observed no spontaneous death in homozygotes out to 9 months of age. When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Wild-type; Wild-type x Heterozygote Coat color: Various Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "The Slc34a1eGFPCre mice express EGFP fused to a constitutively active Cre recombinase protein from the Slc34a1 promoter. The insertion of the eGFPCre cassette abolishes endogenous Slc34a1 expression. Slc34a1 encodes a sodium-dependent inorganic phosphate transporter only expressed only in differentiated kidney epithelial stem cells in the proximal tubule. Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile. Homozygous mice have hypophosphatemia and the donating investigator has observed no lethality in homozygotes out to 9 months of age. When Slc34a1eGFPCre mice are bred with mice containing loxP-flanked sequence, Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the Slc34a1-expressing cells of the offspring. Weak and mosaic EGFP is detectable in S1 and S2 segments of the proximal tubules in the adult kidney, consistent with endogenous expression of Slc34a1. EGFP in this strain is detectable by immunohistochemistry, and is not detectable by direct fluorescence. Of note, a similar strain with tamoxifen-inducible, Cre-mediated recombination driven by the Slc34a1 promoter is available as Stock No. 032285. 分子注记：Using CRISPR technology zygote carrying Slc34a1tm1(EGFP/cre/ERT2)Bhum allele was targeted with sgRNA (GGCGATCTCGAGCCATCTGC) designed to target the cre(ERT2) sequence in the SLC34a1(GCE) mutation to introduce a stop codon after the coding sequence of cre, creating a constitutively active cre-expressing allele."
