      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, hemizygous mice may be bred with wildtype (noncarrier) mice from the colony or with C57BL/6J inbred mice (Stock No. 000664). Homozygous transgenic mice have not been generated by the donating laboratory to date (March 2025). Coat color: Black Generation: \tN8+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Nur77GFP transgenic mice, originally created by Dr. Kristin A. Hogquist (University of Minnesota), express an enhanced green fluorescent protein/codon-optimized \"humanized\" Cre recombinase fusion protein (eGFP-hCre) under control of the Nr4a1 (Nur77) promoter/enhancer regions within the BAC transgene. Specifically, GFP is highly expressed in a subset of myeloid lineage cells of the spleen (but not lymph node), while low levels of GFP are observed in T and B lymphocytes. GFP is up-regulated by antigen receptor stimulation in Nur77GFP transgenic mice, but unlike the CD69 marker of T cell activation, GFP is not induced by inflammatory stimuli. Furthermore, the level of GFP expressed during acute activation reflects the strength of T cell receptor (TCR) stimulation, and the low basal level of GFP expressed in mature na&iuml;ve T cells is dependent on continued interaction with MHC. Dr. Pilar Alcaide purchased some Nur77GFP transgenic animals, on an incipient C57BL/6N background (~N5; Stock No. 016617), and backcrossed these at least 8 generations to the C57BL/6J background (Stock No. 000664). Mice hemizygous for the C57BL/6J Nur77GFP transgene are viable and fertile with normal lymphoid and myeloid development. Homozygous transgenic mice have not been generated by the donating laboratory. The creator of this transgene reports that Cre recombinase activity is observed in all hematopoietic cells at some point in their development (June 2011). Because GFP expression level correlates to the strength of antigen receptor signaling in Nur77GFP transgenic mice, these mice may be useful in studying thymocyte positive- and negative-selection as well as lymphocyte activation; specifically T- and B-cell receptor (TCR and BCR) signal strength perceived by different T- and B-cell subsets during development or activation. In an attempt to offer alleles on well-characterized or multiple genetic backgrounds, alleles are frequently moved to a genetic background different from that on which an allele was first characterized. It should be noted that the phenotype of these C57BL/6J-congenic mice could vary from that originally described on a mixed genetic background. We may modify the strain description if necessary, as published results become available. Of note, this Nur77GFP transgene is also available on an incipient congenic C57BL/6N background (~N5; Stock No. 016617), on a fully C57BL/6N congenic background (~N10+; Stock No. 018974), and on a NOD/ShiLtJ congenic background ("
