      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, heterozygous mice may be bred to wildtype littermates or to C57BL/6J (Stock No. 000664) inbred mice. The donating investigator indicates they have not been able to generate homozygous mice to date (April 2025). Coat color: Black Generation: \tN14+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "The Map2k1 gene encodes a component of the MAP kinase signal transduction pathway, also referred to as MEK1. These MEK1E102_I103del mice harbor a Cre-inducible mutation in exon 3 of the mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase 1 (Map2k1) gene, the mutation results in loss of two amino acids (MEK1 E102_I103del). This is one of the most expressed MEK1 mutations found in human histiocytic tumors and notably resistant to RAS inhibitors. After Cre-mediated recombination, wildtype exon 3 will be excised and the exon 3 harboring the E102_I103del mutations is expressed in cre-expressing tissues. Heterozygous mice are viable and fertile with no overt phenotype. The donating investigator notes that homozygous mice are not produced from heterozygous x heterozygous matings. The expression of wildtype Map2k1 prior to Cre-recombination has not been evaluated to date (April 2025). When MEK1E102_I103del mice are bred to an Mx1-Cre mouse line, the resulting Mx1-Cre;MEK1E102_I103del progeny had a medial survival of ~59 days of age, with development of red cutaneous lesions as well as leukopenia, macrocytic anemia, and thrombocytopenia. These mice may be useful for studying histiocytic cancers. 分子注记：The targeting vector was designed to express a loxP-flanked mutant exon 3, carrying the E102_I103del mutation, of the mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase 1 (Map2k1) gene. The targeting construct consisted of an initial loxP site, wildtype exon 3 sequence, an SV40 polyA sequence, an FRT-flanked neomycin selection cassette, a second loxP site, followed by an inverted mutant exon 3 sequence (c.303_308del; GGAGAT) and a third loxP site in opposite orientation of the second loxP site. FLP recombinase removed the selection cassette."
