      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote; Homozygote x Homozygote Coat color: Black Generation: N20+pN1F2",
      "detailed_desc": "Zip14F/F mice have loxP sites flanking exons 5-8 of the solute carrier family 39 (zinc transporter), member 14 (Slc39a14) gene. Slc39a14 encodes a zinc transporter that mediates the cellular uptake of manganese, zinc, iron, and cadmium that are important for tissue homeostasis, metabolism, development and immunity. Increased expression is induced by proinflammatory stimuli in liver, white adipose tissue, and skeletal muscle. At steady state, Zip14 is located at the basolateral membrane of intestinal epithelial cells (IECs) where it is required to maintain tight junctions and the intestinal permeability. Mice that are homozygous for this allele are viable and fertile. When bred to mice that express tissue-specific Cre recombinase, resulting offspring will have exons 5-8 deleted in the cre-expressing tissues. When bred to Villin-Cre mice (Stock No. 004586), resulting enterocyte-specific Zip14&Delta;IEC mice exhibit selective dysbiosis and differential expression of tight junction proteins, claudin 1 and 2, and specific cytokines associated with intestinal inflammation. HDAC activity and zinc uptake are also reduced. 分子注记：LoxP sites were inserted in introns 4 and 8 via CRISPR/Cas9 technology."
