      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, these mice can be bred as homozygotes. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Generation: ?+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "3xMetRS* is an improved version of STOPflox R26-MetRS* (1xMetRS*; Stock No. 028071) carrying three copies of methionyl-tRNA synthetase 1 with L274G point mutation (Mars1). The mutation results in an expanded binding site that enables loading of the non-canonical amino-acid methionine analogs, azidonorleucine (ANL), onto methionine tRNA. As endogenous wildtype methionyl-tRNA synthetase does not bind ANL, only expression of the mutant MetRS (MetRS*) allows the incorporation of ANL into nascent proteins. They can then be subsequently labeled by fluorescent non-canonical amino-acid tagging (FUNCAT) or bioorthogonal non-canonical amino acid tagging (BONCAT) for imaging or purification, respectively. STOPflox R26-3xMetRS* mice were generated by knocking in a floxed STOP cassette, three copies of the mutant Mars1 sequence, and one copy of EGFP per allele, all under the control of a CAG promoter with all four parts separated by different self-cleaving 2A peptides, into the endogenous Gt(ROSA)26Sor locus. The 2A sequence enables the expression of the three copies of mutant Mars1 and EGFP as discrete translation products from a single promoter. Following Cre recombinase-mediated removal of the floxed STOP cassette, EGFP expression and ANL incorporation are only detected in cells expressing the mutant methionine-tRNA synthetase, MetRS* (Mars1*). Mice that are heterozygous or homozygous for the knock-in allele are viable and fertile. Both heterozygous and homozygous mice showed no obvious behavioral differences with wild-type mice. Compared to 1xMetRS* (Stock No. 028071), the 3xMetRS* mouse line allows faster and more efficient labelling with the non-canonical amino acid ANL and does not need a low methionine diet for labelling. It works for labelling in the heterozygous state (3xMetRS*) as well as the homozygous state (6xMetRS*) when activated by Cre-mediated excision of the floxed STOP. When bred to a strain with cell type-specific Cre recombinase expression, it can be used for studies on cell type-specific proteomes, protein synthesis, or degradation in any tissue. Of note, strains containing mutant aminoacyl-tRNA synthetases that recognize azide-bearing noncanonical amino acids include: MetRS* (Stock No. 028071), PheRS* (Stock No. 033734), and TyrRS* (Stock No. 033735). MetRS* (Stock No. 028071) is the original strain with single 1xMetRS*.&nbsp; 分子注记：The allele consists of the CAG, floxed STOP-MetRS(L274G)-T2A-MetRS(L274G)-P2A-MetRS(L274G)-E2A-EGFP (WPRE ) inserte"
