      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygotes may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Scube2-creER knock-in mice have the cre-ERT2 sequence inserted into the 3' UTR of the signal peptide, CUB domain, EGF-like 2 (Scube2) gene. These mice express cre/ERT2 specifically in alveolar fibroblasts in the lung. Restricted to the cytoplasm, cre-ERT2 can only gain access to the nuclear compartment after exposure to tamoxifen. Homozygotes are viable and fertile with no overt phenotype. The donating laboratory reports that the endogenous SCUBE2 expression from the Scube2-creER allele seems reduced compared to the wild type allele, most likely because of the alteration in the 3' end of mRNA. When these mice are bred with mice containing a loxP-flanked sequence, tamoxifen-inducible Cre-mediated recombination will result in deletion of the floxed sequences in the Cre-expressing cells of the offspring. 分子注记：Using CRISPR/Cas9 technology, a P2A-CreERT2-stop codon-rabbit beta globin polyA sequence was inserted into exon 22 of the Scube2 gene."
