      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Heterozygote x Heterozygote Coat color: Black Generation: +pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "Camk2d codes for one of the calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase type 2 (CAMK2) family isoforms. CAMKII&delta; is expressed in the heart and has been associated with cardiac development and function. Oxidative stress may result in CAMKII&delta; dysregulation and ultimately lead to cardiac failure. Specifically, oxidization at cysteine (Cys273/Cys290) residues and disulfide formation in in CAMKII&delta;'s regulatory domain results in calcium/calmodulin independent activity. These Camk2dCys273S knock-in (KI) mice express a mutant CAMKII&delta; that has an amino acid substitution of cysteine to a serine at residue 273 to prevent disulfide formation between the Cys273 and Cys290 residues. Homozygous mice are viable and fertile with no over phenotype. Camk2dCys273S KI mice are less suspectable to cardiac dysfunction after ischemia-reperfusion injury. These mice may be useful when studying the regulatory role of CAMKII&delta; in cardiac function and disease. 分子注记：Using CRISPR/Cas9 endonuclease-mediated genome editing, a single guide RNA (AGTGACTTACACAGATCCAT) and a single-strand oligo donor template was used to introduce a point mutation that produces an amino acid substitution of cysteine to serine at position 273 (Cys273S) in the calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase II, delta (Camk2d) gene."
