      "breeding_summary": "When maintaining a live colony, homozygous mice may be bred together. Mating scheme: Homozygote x Homozygote Generation: N6+pN1",
      "detailed_desc": "LSL-ERTurboID knock-in mice have CAG promoter directing Cre-inducible expression of an HA- and V5-tagged endoplasmic reticulum-directed biotin ligase sequence, ERTurboID, inserted into the Igs2 locus. Cre-mediated recombination results in the excision of a floxed STOP cassette, enabling the tissue and time-dependent expression of ERTurboID. In these LSL-ERTurboID, a floxed STOP cassette blocks downstream expression of the ERTurboID cassette. After breeding to a Cre-expressing line, these mice secrete biotinylated proteins in a tissue-specific fashion when given exogenous biotin in their diet. This allows highly specific biotinylation and purification of proteins trafficking through the secretory pathway and permits the analysis of cellular secretomes through streptavidin affinity purification and quantitative mass spectrometry proteomics. Homozygous mice are viable and fertile. 分子注记：Site-specific PhiC31 integrase-mediated transgenesis is used to insert an LSL-ERTurboID into the intergenic site 2 locus (Hipp11). The targeting vector used for the Igs2 TARGATT site-specific Phi C31 integrase-mediated cassette exchange consists of from 5' to 3', a CMV-IE enhancer/chicken beta-actin/rabbit beta-globin hybrid promoter (from pCAGGS), a floxed STOP cassette containing 3 SV40 late polyA signals, an HA- and V5-tagged biotin ligase sequence fused to an endoplasmic reticulum-targeting Igk leader sequence, and an endoplasmic reticulum retention signal (RDEL). The construct was microinjected, along with the PhiC31 integrase mRNA, into the pronuclei of zygotes collected from TARGATT B6J/H11-attP3 mice on a C57BL/6J genetic background."
